{"task_id": "HumanEval/5", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef intersperse(numbers: List[int], delimeter: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Insert a number 'delimeter' between every two consecutive elements of input list `numbers`.\n    The function returns a new list with the delimiter inserted.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return []\n\n    result: List[int] = []\n    for i, val in enumerate(numbers):\n        result.append(val)\n        if i < len(numbers) - 1:\n            result.append(delimeter)\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/6", "solution": "def parse_nested_parens(paren_string: str) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Computes the deepest nesting level for parentheses in each space-separated group.\n    Ignores non-parenthesis characters and handles unbalanced groups by allowing depth to go negative.\"\"\"\n    \n    results = []\n    groups = paren_string.split()\n\n    for group in groups:\n        current_depth = 0\n        max_depth = 0\n        for char in group:\n            if char == '(':\n                current_depth += 1\n                if current_depth > max_depth:\n                    max_depth = current_depth\n            elif char == ')':\n                current_depth -= 1\n        results.append(max_depth)\n    \n    return results"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/6", "solution": "from typing import List\n\n\ndef parse_nested_parens(paren_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Input is a string of parenthesis groups. Returns deepest nesting per group.\n    Assumes well-formed, balanced parenthesis groups containing only '(' and ')' characters.\"\"\"\n\n    groups = [g for g in paren_string.split() if g]\n\n    results = []\n    for group in groups:\n        current_depth = 0\n        max_depth = 0\n        for char in group:\n            if char == '(':\n                current_depth += 1\n                if current_depth > max_depth:\n                    max_depth = current_depth\n            else:  # Assumes char is ')' due to critical requirements\n                current_depth -= 1\n        results.append(max_depth)\n\n    return results"}
