{"task_id": "HumanEval/16", "solution": "```python\nimport collections\n\n# Global cache to fulfill the in-memory, process-lifetime caching requirement.\n# This acts as the CacheRepository for the bare function, adhering to FIFO eviction.\n_cache = collections.OrderedDict()\n_MAX_CACHE_SIZE = 1000\n\n\ndef count_distinct_characters(string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Given a string, find out how many distinct characters (regardless of case) does it consist of.\n    This function processes the input string and uses a global in-memory cache for performance.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Normalize string to canonical case, using casefold for robust case-insensitivity.\n    normalized_string = string.casefold()\n\n    # Consult the cache for a pre-computed result.\n    if normalized_string in _cache:\n        return _cache[normalized_string]\n\n    # Compute the distinct character count if not found in cache.\n    count = len(set(normalized_string))\n\n    # Store the new result in the cache, applying FIFO eviction if max size is exceeded.\n    _cache[normalized_string] = count\n    if len(_cache) > _MAX_CACHE_SIZE:\n        _cache.popitem(last=False)  # Remove the oldest entry\n\n    return count\n```"}
