{"task_id": "HumanEval/28", "solution": "```python\n# pyproject.toml\n# Note: This is a placeholder for a pyproject.toml file.\n# The content below should be placed in a file named `pyproject.toml` at the project root.\n\"\"\"\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"strconcat\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A simple Python library to concatenate lists of strings.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"strconcat\", from = \"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \">=3.8\"\nfastapi = \"^0.111.0\"\nuvicorn = {extras = [\"standard\"], version = \"^0.30.1\"}\npydantic = \"^2.7.4\"\nuuid = \"^1.30\"\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^8.2.2\"\npytest-cov = \"^5.0.0\"\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\nstrconcat = \"scripts.cli_entry:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\"\"\"\n\n# README.md\n# Note: This is a placeholder for a README.md file.\n# The content below should be placed in a file named `README.md` at the project root.\n\"\"\"\n# StrConcat\n\nA small, well-tested Python library and optional interfaces to concatenate lists of strings into a single string.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install strconcat\n```\n\nOr, if you use Poetry:\n\n```bash\npoetry add strconcat\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Programmatic\n\n```python\nfrom strconcat.concatenator import Concatenator\nfrom strconcat.repository import InMemoryAuditRepository # for example, or AuditRepository()\n\naudit_repo = InMemoryAuditRepository() # Or AuditRepository() for file-based\nconcatenator = Concatenator(audit_repo=audit_repo)\n\nresult = concatenator.concatenate([\"hello\", \"world\"])\nprint(result) # Output: helloworld\n\ntry:\n    concatenator.concatenate([\"hello\", 123])\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(e) # Output: strings must be List[str]\n```\n\n### CLI\n\nThe `strconcat` command-line tool is installed with the package.\n\n```bash\n# Concatenate arguments\nstrconcat hello world\n# Output: helloworld\n\n# Concatenate from stdin (use '-' argument)\necho -e \"first\\nsecond\\nthird\" | strconcat -\n# Output: firstsecondthird\n\n# Empty input\nstrconcat\n# Output:\n\n# Invalid input will show an error message and exit with code 2\nstrconcat hello 123\n# Output: Error: strings must be List[str]\n```\n\n### HTTP API\n\nAn optional HTTP API can be run using Uvicorn.\n\n```bash\n# Set an optional API key if desired (recommended for production)\n# export STRCONCAT_API_KEY=\"mysecretkey\"\n\nuvicorn strconcat.controllers:create_api_app --factory --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n\nThen, you can make POST requests:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:8000/concatenate \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"strings\": [\"alpha\", \"beta\"]}'\n# Output: {\"result\":\"alphabeta\"}\n```\n\nWith an API key set:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:8000/concatenate \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -H \"X-API-Key: mysecretkey\" \\\n     -d '{\"strings\": [\"alpha\", \"beta\"]}'\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\nEnvironment variables can be used to configure the application:\n\n- `STRCONCAT_AUDIT_LOG_PATH`: Path to the JSONL audit log file (default: `strconcat_audit.jsonl`).\n- `STRCONCAT_API_KEY`: API key for the HTTP API (if set, `X-API-Key` header is required).\n\n## Audit Logs\n\nAudit records are stored in a JSONL file (default: `strconcat_audit.jsonl`) or in an in-memory repository for testing.\nEach line is a JSON object:\n\n```json\n{\"request_id\": \"...\", \"timestamp\": \"...\", \"input_count\": 2, \"result_length\": 9, \"source\": \"api\"}\n```\n\"\"\"\n\n# src/strconcat/__init__.py\nimport logging\nfrom .config import Config\n\n# Configure basic logging for the library\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format='%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n\n# Load configuration from environment variables on package import.\nConfig.load_from_env()\n\n# Explicitly define what gets imported when someone does `from strconcat import ...`\n# This can be refined based on what public API elements are most commonly used.\nfrom .concatenator import Concatenator\nfrom .repository import AuditRepository, InMemoryAuditRepository\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom .models import AuditRecord, ConcatenateRequest, ConcatenateResponse\nfrom .controllers import create_api_app, CLIController\n\n# This makes the main concatenate function directly available for a simplified import.\n# However, the design implies using the Concatenator class.\n# For consistency with the design, we expose the class.\n# The original problem statement had a single function, but the spec has a class.\n# I will stick to the spec's class design.\n\n\n# src/strconcat/config.py\nimport os\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nclass Config:\n    \"\"\"Central configuration values and loading from environment variables.\"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_SEPARATOR: str = \"\"\n    AUDIT_LOG_PATH: str = \"strconcat_audit.jsonl\"\n    API_KEY: Optional[str] = None\n\n    @classmethod\n    def load_from_env(cls) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Load configuration overrides from environment variables.\"\"\"\n        cls.AUDIT_LOG_PATH = os.getenv(\"STRCONCAT_AUDIT_LOG_PATH\", cls.AUDIT_LOG_PATH)\n        cls.API_KEY = os.getenv(\"STRCONCAT_API_KEY\")\n\n\n# src/strconcat/models.py\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nclass ConcatenateRequest(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Data transfer object for a concatenation request.\"\"\"\n    strings: List[str]\n    source: Optional[str] = None\n\nclass ConcatenateResponse(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Data transfer object for a concatenation response.\"\"\"\n    result: str\n\nclass AuditRecord(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Domain model for an audit record.\"\"\"\n    request_id: str\n    timestamp: str\n    input_count: int\n    result_length: int\n    source: str\n\n\n# src/strconcat/exceptions.py\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Application-specific exception for invalid input.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Invalid input.\"):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\n\n# src/strconcat/utils.py\nimport uuid\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef validate_strings(strings: List[Any]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Ensures input is a list of strings.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(strings, list):\n        return False\n    return all(isinstance(s, str) for s in strings)\n\ndef gen_request_id() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Generates a UUID string for request identification.\"\"\"\n    return str(uuid.uuid4())\n\ndef now_iso() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Returns the current UTC timestamp in ISO8601 format.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.utcnow().isoformat() + \"Z\"\n\n\n# src/strconcat/repository.py\nimport json\nimport logging\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom strconcat.models import AuditRecord\nfrom strconcat.config import Config\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass AuditRepository:\n    \"\"\"Persists audit records to a JSONL file.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, path: str = Config.AUDIT_LOG_PATH) -> None:\n        self.path = path\n\n    def store(self, record: AuditRecord) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Appends a single audit record as a JSON line to the file.\"\"\"\n        line = json.dumps(record.model_dump(), ensure_ascii=False)\n        with open(self.path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            f.write(line + \"\\n\")\n\n    def get_all(self) -> List[AuditRecord]:\n        \"\"\"Reads all audit records from the JSONL file.\"\"\"\n        records: List[AuditRecord] = []\n        try:\n            with open(self.path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                for line in f:\n                    try:\n                        data = json.loads(line)\n                        records.append(AuditRecord(**data))\n                    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n                        logger.warning(f\"Skipping malformed audit log line: {line.strip()}. Error: {e}\")\n        except FileNotFoundError:\n            pass # No audit file yet, return empty list\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Error reading audit log file {self.path}: {e}\")\n        return records\n\nclass InMemoryAuditRepository(AuditRepository):\n    \"\"\"An in-memory audit repository for testing purposes.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        self.records: List[AuditRecord] = []\n\n    def store(self, record: AuditRecord) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Appends an audit record to the in-memory list.\"\"\"\n        self.records.append(record)\n\n    def get_all(self) -> List[AuditRecord]:\n        \"\"\"Returns a copy of all in-memory audit records.\"\"\"\n        return list(self.records)\n\n\n# src/strconcat/concatenator.py\nimport logging\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom strconcat import utils, models\nfrom strconcat.repository import AuditRepository\nfrom strconcat.exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom strconcat.config import Config\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass Concatenator:\n    \"\"\"Core service for concatenating strings and auditing operations.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, separator: str = Config.DEFAULT_SEPARATOR, audit_repo: Optional[AuditRepository] = None) -> None:\n        self.separator = separator\n        self.audit_repo = audit_repo\n\n    def concatenate(self, strings: List[str], source: Optional[str] = \"programmatic\") -> str:\n        \"\"\"Concatenates a list of strings into a single string, with audit.\"\"\"\n        if not utils.validate_strings(strings):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"strings must be List[str]\")\n\n        result = self.separator.join(strings)\n\n        record = models.AuditRecord(\n            request_id=utils.gen_request_id(),\n            timestamp=utils.now_iso(),\n            input_count=len(strings),\n            result_length=len(result),\n            source=source if source else \"programmatic\"\n        )\n        try:\n            if self.audit_repo:\n                self.audit_repo.store(record)\n        except Exception:\n            logger.exception(\"Failed to persist audit record (non-fatal).\")\n        return result\n\n\n# src/strconcat/controllers.py\nimport sys\nimport logging\nimport argparse\nimport uvicorn\nfrom typing import List, Optional, Callable\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, Header, Depends, status\n\nfrom strconcat import models, utils\nfrom strconcat.concatenator import Concatenator\nfrom strconcat.repository import AuditRepository\nfrom strconcat.exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom strconcat.config import Config\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Controller for the command-line interface.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, concatenator: Concatenator) -> None:\n        self.concatenator = concatenator\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Parses arguments, calls concatenation logic, and prints result.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            description=\"Concatenate a list of strings.\",\n            formatter_class=argparse.RawTextHelpFormatter\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            'strings',\n            nargs='*',\n            help=\"Strings to concatenate. Use '-' to read from stdin (one string per line).\"\n        )\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n        input_strings: List[str] = []\n        if '-' in args.strings:\n            if len(args.strings) > 1:\n                print(\"Error: Cannot combine stdin ('-') with other arguments.\", file=sys.stderr)\n                return 2\n            input_strings = [line.strip() for line in sys.stdin if line.strip()]\n        else:\n            input_strings = args.strings\n\n        try:\n            result = self.concatenator.concatenate(input_strings, source=\"cli\")\n            print(result)\n            return 0\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.exception(\"An unexpected error occurred in CLI.\")\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\n\ndef create_api_app(audit_repo: Optional[AuditRepository] = None) -> FastAPI:\n    \"\"\"Builds and configures a FastAPI application for the HTTP API.\"\"\"\n    app = FastAPI(\n        title=\"StrConcat API\",\n        description=\"API to concatenate lists of strings.\",\n        version=\"0.1.0\"\n    )\n\n    if audit_repo is None:\n        audit_repo = AuditRepository(path=Config.AUDIT_LOG_PATH)\n    concatenator = Concatenator(audit_repo=audit_repo)\n\n    def verify_api_key(x_api_key: Optional[str] = Header(None)) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Dependency for API key authentication.\"\"\"\n        if Config.API_KEY is not None:\n            if x_api_key != Config.API_KEY:\n                raise HTTPException(\n                    status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n                    detail=\"Invalid or missing API Key\"\n                )\n        return True\n\n    @app.post(\"/concatenate\", response_model=models.ConcatenateResponse)\n    async def post_concatenate(\n        request: models.ConcatenateRequest,\n        api_key_verified: bool = Depends(verify_api_key)\n    ) -> models.ConcatenateResponse:\n        \"\"\"\n        Concatenates a list of strings provided in the request body.\n        Requires an API key if STRCONCAT_API_KEY environment variable is set.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            result = concatenator.concatenate(request.strings, source=\"api\")\n            return models.ConcatenateResponse(result=result)\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=str(e))\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.exception(\"An unexpected error occurred in API endpoint.\")\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"Internal server error\")\n\n    return app\n\n\n# src/strconcat/testsupport.py\n# This file is intended for test helpers. As InMemoryAuditRepository is directly\n# in repository.py as per design, this file can serve for other utilities or be\n# kept for future expansion. For now, it will be empty or re-export.\nfrom strconcat.repository import InMemoryAuditRepository\n\n# Potentially, a factory function for InMemoryAuditRepository could live here\n# if it were more complex, but a direct import is sufficient for now.\n\n\n# scripts/cli_entry.py\nimport sys\nfrom strconcat.controllers import CLIController\nfrom strconcat.concatenator import Concatenator\nfrom strconcat.repository import AuditRepository\nfrom strconcat.config import Config\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"Main entry point for the CLI script.\"\"\"\n    # Ensure config is loaded before instantiating components\n    Config.load_from_env()\n\n    audit_repo = AuditRepository(path=Config.AUDIT_LOG_PATH)\n    concatenator = Concatenator(audit_repo=audit_repo)\n    cli_controller = CLIController(concatenator=concatenator)\n    sys.exit(cli_controller.run(sys.argv[1:]))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n\n# tests/test_concatenator.py\nimport pytest\nfrom typing import List\n\nfrom strconcat.concatenator import Concatenator\nfrom strconcat.exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom strconcat.repository import InMemoryAuditRepository\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef in_memory_concatenator():\n    \"\"\"Provides a Concatenator instance with an in-memory audit repository.\"\"\"\n    repo = InMemoryAuditRepository()\n    return Concatenator(audit_repo=repo), repo\n\ndef test_concatenate_empty_list(in_memory_concatenator):\n    \"\"\"Tests concatenation of an empty list.\"\"\"\n    concatenator, repo = in_memory_concatenator\n    result = concatenator.concatenate([])\n    assert result == \"\"\n    assert len(repo.get_all()) == 1\n    assert repo.get_all()[0].input_count == 0\n    assert repo.get_all()[0].result_length == 0\n\ndef test_concatenate_basic_list(in_memory_concatenator):\n    \"\"\"Tests concatenation of a simple list of strings.\"\"\"\n    concatenator, repo = in_memory_concatenator\n    strings = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]\n    result = concatenator.concatenate(strings)\n    assert result == \"abc\"\n    assert len(repo.get_all()) == 1\n    assert repo.get_all()[0].input_count == 3\n    assert repo.get_all()[0].result_length == 3\n\ndef test_concatenate_with_separator(in_memory_concatenator):\n    \"\"\"Tests concatenation with a custom separator.\"\"\"\n    repo = InMemoryAuditRepository()\n    concatenator = Concatenator(separator=\"-\", audit_repo=repo)\n    strings = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n    result = concatenator.concatenate(strings)\n    assert result == \"apple-banana-cherry\"\n    assert len(repo.get_all()) == 1\n    assert repo.get_all()[0].input_count == 3\n    assert repo.get_all()[0].result_length == len(\"apple-banana-cherry\")\n\n\ndef test_concatenate_single_string(in_memory_concatenator):\n    \"\"\"Tests concatenation of a list with a single string.\"\"\"\n    concatenator, repo = in_memory_concatenator\n    strings = [\"hello\"]\n    result = concatenator.concatenate(strings)\n    assert result == \"hello\"\n    assert len(repo.get_all()) == 1\n    assert repo.get_all()[0].input_count == 1\n    assert repo.get_all()[0].result_length == 5\n\ndef test_concatenate_large_list(in_memory_concatenator):\n    \"\"\"Tests concatenation with a large number of strings.\"\"\"\n    concatenator, repo = in_memory_concatenator\n    strings = [str(i) for i in range(1000)]\n    result = concatenator.concatenate(strings)\n    assert len(result) == sum(len(s) for s in strings)\n    assert result == \"\".join(strings)\n    assert len(repo.get_all()) == 1\n    assert repo.get_all()[0].input_count == 1000\n    assert repo.get_all()[0].result_length == len(result)\n\ndef test_concatenate_raises_on_non_list_input(in_memory_concatenator):\n    \"\"\"Ensures InvalidInputError is raised for non-list input.\"\"\"\n    concatenator, _ = in_memory_concatenator\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"strings must be List[str]\"):\n        concatenator.concatenate(\"not a list\") # type: ignore\n\ndef test_concatenate_raises_on_list_with_non_str_elements(in_memory_concatenator):\n    \"\"\"Ensures InvalidInputError is raised for list containing non-string elements.\"\"\"\n    concatenator, _ = in_memory_concatenator\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"strings must be List[str]\"):\n        concatenator.concatenate([\"a\", 123, \"c\"]) # type: ignore\n\ndef test_concatenate_raises_on_list_with_none_elements(in_memory_concatenator):\n    \"\"\"Ensures InvalidInputError is raised for list containing None elements.\"\"\"\n    concatenator, _ = in_memory_concatenator\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"strings must be List[str]\"):\n        concatenator.concatenate([\"a\", None, \"c\"]) # type: ignore\n\ndef test_audit_record_content(in_memory_concatenator):\n    \"\"\"Verifies the content of the stored audit record.\"\"\"\n    concatenator, repo = in_memory_concatenator\n    strings = [\"test\", \"audit\"]\n    result = concatenator.concatenate(strings, source=\"programmatic_test\")\n    record = repo.get_all()[0]\n    assert record.input_count == 2\n    assert record.result_length == len(result)\n    assert record.source == \"programmatic_test\"\n    assert record.request_id is not None\n    assert record.timestamp is not None\n\ndef test_no_audit_if_repo_none():\n    \"\"\"Tests that no audit record is stored if no repository is provided.\"\"\"\n    concatenator = Concatenator()\n    concatenator.concatenate([\"a\", \"b\"]) # No repo, no exception expected\n    # No way to assert no store was called without mocking, but behavior is verified by\n    # the fact that in_memory_concatenator fixture always gives a repo.\n    # This test simply ensures no crash.\n\n\n# tests/test_repository.py\nimport pytest\nimport os\nimport json\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom strconcat.repository import AuditRepository, InMemoryAuditRepository\nfrom strconcat.models import AuditRecord\nfrom strconcat.utils import now_iso, gen_request_id\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef temp_audit_file(tmp_path):\n    \"\"\"Provides a temporary file path for AuditRepository tests.\"\"\"\n    file_path = tmp_path / \"test_audit.jsonl\"\n    yield file_path\n    if file_path.exists():\n        os.remove(file_path)\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef sample_audit_record():\n    \"\"\"Provides a sample AuditRecord for testing.\"\"\"\n    return AuditRecord(\n        request_id=gen_request_id(),\n        timestamp=now_iso(),\n        input_count=3,\n        result_length=6,\n        source=\"test\"\n    )\n\nclass TestAuditRepository:\n    \"\"\"Tests for the file-based AuditRepository.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_store_record_creates_file_if_not_exists(self, temp_audit_file, sample_audit_record):\n        \"\"\"Ensures store() creates the audit file if it doesn't exist.\"\"\"\n        repo = AuditRepository(path=temp_audit_file)\n        repo.store(sample_audit_record)\n        assert temp_audit_file.exists()\n\n    def test_store_record_appends_to_file(self, temp_audit_file, sample_audit_record):\n        \"\"\"Ensures store() appends new records to the audit file.\"\"\"\n        repo = AuditRepository(path=temp_audit_file)\n        repo.store(sample_audit_record)\n        \n        second_record = AuditRecord(\n            request_id=gen_request_id(),\n            timestamp=now_iso(),\n            input_count=2,\n            result_length=5,\n            source=\"another_test\"\n        )\n        repo.store(second_record)\n\n        with open(temp_audit_file, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            lines = f.readlines()\n            assert len(lines) == 2\n            assert json.loads(lines[0]) == sample_audit_record.model_dump()\n            assert json.loads(lines[1]) == second_record.model_dump()\n\n    def test_get_all_returns_empty_list_if_file_not_exists(self, temp_audit_file):\n        \"\"\"Ensures get_all() returns an empty list if the audit file does not exist.\"\"\"\n        repo = AuditRepository(path=temp_audit_file)\n        records = repo.get_all()\n        assert records == []\n\n    def test_get_all_retrieves_all_records(self, temp_audit_file, sample_audit_record):\n        \"\"\"Ensures get_all() retrieves all stored records correctly.\"\"\"\n        repo = AuditRepository(path=temp_audit_file)\n        repo.store(sample_audit_record)\n        \n        second_record = AuditRecord(\n            request_id=gen_request_id(),\n            timestamp=now_iso(),\n            input_count=2,\n            result_length=5,\n            source=\"another_test\"\n        )\n        repo.store(second_record)\n\n        retrieved_records = repo.get_all()\n        assert len(retrieved_records) == 2\n        assert retrieved_records[0] == sample_audit_record\n        assert retrieved_records[1] == second_record\n\n    def test_get_all_handles_malformed_lines(self, temp_audit_file, caplog):\n        \"\"\"Ensures get_all() logs a warning and skips malformed lines.\"\"\"\n        repo = AuditRepository(path=temp_audit_file)\n        with open(temp_audit_file, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            f.write(\"{\\\"valid_record\\\": true}\\n\")\n            f.write(\"this is not json\\n\")\n            f.write(\"{\\\"another_valid\\\": true}\\n\")\n        \n        with caplog.at_level('WARNING'):\n            records = repo.get_all()\n            assert len(records) == 2 # Only valid records should be parsed\n            assert \"Skipping malformed audit log line\" in caplog.text\n\nclass TestInMemoryAuditRepository:\n    \"\"\"Tests for the in-memory AuditRepository.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_store_record_appends_to_list(self, sample_audit_record):\n        \"\"\"Ensures store() appends records to the in-memory list.\"\"\"\n        repo = InMemoryAuditRepository()\n        repo.store(sample_audit_record)\n        assert len(repo.records) == 1\n        assert repo.records[0] == sample_audit_record\n\n    def test_get_all_returns_all_records(self, sample_audit_record):\n        \"\"\"Ensures get_all() returns all records from the in-memory list.\"\"\"\n        repo = InMemoryAuditRepository()\n        repo.store(sample_audit_record)\n        \n        second_record = AuditRecord(\n            request_id=gen_request_id(),\n            timestamp=now_iso(),\n            input_count=2,\n            result_length=5,\n            source=\"another_test_in_mem\"\n        )\n        repo.store(second_record)\n\n        retrieved_records = repo.get_all()\n        assert len(retrieved_records) == 2\n        assert retrieved_records[0] == sample_audit_record\n        assert retrieved_records[1] == second_record\n\n    def test_get_all_returns_copy_of_records(self, sample_audit_record):\n        \"\"\"Ensures get_all() returns a copy to prevent external modification.\"\"\"\n        repo = InMemoryAuditRepository()\n        repo.store(sample_audit_record)\n        retrieved_records = repo.get_all()\n        \n        # Modify the retrieved list, it should not affect the original in the repo\n        retrieved_records.append(sample_audit_record) \n        assert len(repo.records) == 1\n        assert len(retrieved_records) == 2\n\n\n# tests/test_cli.py\nimport pytest\nfrom unittest.mock import patch, MagicMock\nfrom io import StringIO\nimport sys\n\nfrom strconcat.controllers import CLIController\nfrom strconcat.concatenator import Concatenator\nfrom strconcat.exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom strconcat.repository import InMemoryAuditRepository\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef mock_concatenator():\n    \"\"\"Mocks the Concatenator for CLIController tests.\"\"\"\n    mock = MagicMock(spec=Concatenator)\n    mock.concatenate.return_value = \"concatenated_result\"\n    return mock\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef cli_controller(mock_concatenator):\n    \"\"\"Provides a CLIController instance with a mocked concatenator.\"\"\"\n    return CLIController(concatenator=mock_concatenator)\n\n@pytest.fixture(autouse=True)\ndef capture_stdout_stderr():\n    \"\"\"Captures stdout and stderr during tests.\"\"\"\n    old_stdout = sys.stdout\n    old_stderr = sys.stderr\n    sys.stdout = StringIO()\n    sys.stderr = StringIO()\n    yield sys.stdout, sys.stderr\n    sys.stdout = old_stdout\n    sys.stderr = old_stderr\n\ndef test_cli_empty_args(cli_controller, mock_concatenator, capture_stdout_stderr):\n    \"\"\"Tests CLI with no arguments, expecting an empty string result.\"\"\"\n    stdout, _ = capture_stdout_stderr\n    mock_concatenator.concatenate.return_value = \"\" # Default for empty list\n    exit_code = cli_controller.run([])\n    assert exit_code == 0\n    assert stdout.getvalue().strip() == \"\"\n    mock_concatenator.concatenate.assert_called_once_with([], source=\"cli\")\n\ndef test_cli_with_string_args(cli_controller, mock_concatenator, capture_stdout_stderr):\n    \"\"\"Tests CLI with multiple string arguments.\"\"\"\n    stdout, _ = capture_stdout_stderr\n    args = [\"hello\", \"world\"]\n    exit_code = cli_controller.run(args)\n    assert exit_code == 0\n    assert stdout.getvalue().strip() == \"concatenated_result\"\n    mock_concatenator.concatenate.assert_called_once_with(args, source=\"cli\")\n\ndef test_cli_with_invalid_input(cli_controller, mock_concatenator, capture_stdout_stderr):\n    \"\"\"Tests CLI behavior on InvalidInputError.\"\"\"\n    _, stderr = capture_stdout_stderr\n    mock_concatenator.concatenate.side_effect = InvalidInputError(\"test error\")\n    args = [\"a\", \"123\"] # This input would normally cause an error\n    exit_code = cli_controller.run(args)\n    assert exit_code == 2\n    assert \"Error: test error\" in stderr.getvalue()\n    mock_concatenator.concatenate.assert_called_once_with(args, source=\"cli\")\n\ndef test_cli_read_from_stdin(cli_controller, mock_concatenator, capture_stdout_stderr):\n    \"\"\"Tests CLI reading input from stdin.\"\"\"\n    stdout, _ = capture_stdout_stderr\n    mock_stdin = StringIO(\"line1\\nline2\\nline3\\n\")\n    with patch('sys.stdin', mock_stdin):\n        exit_code = cli_controller.run([\"-\"])\n    assert exit_code == 0\n    assert stdout.getvalue().strip() == \"concatenated_result\"\n    mock_concatenator.concatenate.assert_called_once_with([\"line1\", \"line2\", \"line3\"], source=\"cli\")\n\ndef test_cli_read_from_stdin_with_empty_lines(cli_controller, mock_concatenator, capture_stdout_stderr):\n    \"\"\"Tests CLI reading from stdin with empty lines.\"\"\"\n    stdout, _ = capture_stdout_stderr\n    mock_stdin = StringIO(\"line1\\n\\nline2\\n\")\n    with patch('sys.stdin', mock_stdin):\n        exit_code = cli_controller.run([\"-\"])\n    assert exit_code == 0\n    assert stdout.getvalue().strip() == \"concatenated_result\"\n    mock_concatenator.concatenate.assert_called_once_with([\"line1\", \"line2\"], source=\"cli\")\n\ndef test_cli_read_from_stdin_and_args_error(cli_controller, mock_concatenator, capture_stdout_stderr):\n    \"\"\"Tests CLI error when stdin and other args are provided.\"\"\"\n    _, stderr = capture_stdout_stderr\n    exit_code = cli_controller.run([\"-\", \"some_arg\"])\n    assert exit_code == 2\n    assert \"Error: Cannot combine stdin ('-') with other arguments.\" in stderr.getvalue()\n    mock_concatenator.concatenate.assert_not_called()\n\ndef test_cli_unexpected_error(cli_controller, mock_concatenator, caplog, capture_stdout_stderr):\n    \"\"\"Tests CLI behavior on an unexpected internal error.\"\"\"\n    _, stderr = capture_stdout_stderr\n    mock_concatenator.concatenate.side_effect = RuntimeError(\"unexpected issue\")\n    \n    with caplog.at_level('ERROR'):\n        exit_code = cli_controller.run([\"a\", \"b\"])\n        \n    assert exit_code == 1\n    assert \"An unexpected error occurred: unexpected issue\" in stderr.getvalue()\n    assert \"An unexpected error occurred in CLI.\" in caplog.text\n\n\n# tests/test_api.py\nimport pytest\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\nfrom unittest.mock import MagicMock\n\nfrom strconcat.controllers import create_api_app\nfrom strconcat.repository import InMemoryAuditRepository\nfrom strconcat.concatenator import Concatenator\nfrom strconcat.exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom strconcat.config import Config\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef in_memory_audit_repo():\n    \"\"\"Provides an in-memory audit repository for API tests.\"\"\"\n    return InMemoryAuditRepository()\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef client_no_api_key(in_memory_audit_repo):\n    \"\"\"Provides a TestClient for the API without API key enforcement.\"\"\"\n    # Temporarily set API_KEY to None to disable it for this fixture\n    original_api_key = Config.API_KEY\n    Config.API_KEY = None\n    app = create_api_app(audit_repo=in_memory_audit_repo)\n    yield TestClient(app)\n    Config.API_KEY = original_api_key # Restore original state\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef client_with_api_key(in_memory_audit_repo):\n    \"\"\"Provides a TestClient for the API with API key enforcement.\"\"\"\n    # Temporarily set API_KEY for this fixture\n    original_api_key = Config.API_KEY\n    Config.API_KEY = \"test_api_key\"\n    app = create_api_app(audit_repo=in_memory_audit_repo)\n    yield TestClient(app)\n    Config.API_KEY = original_api_key # Restore original state\n\nclass TestAPIConcatenate:\n    \"\"\"Integration tests for the HTTP POST /concatenate endpoint.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_post_concatenate_success(self, client_no_api_key, in_memory_audit_repo):\n        \"\"\"Tests successful concatenation via the API.\"\"\"\n        response = client_no_api_key.post(\"/concatenate\", json={\"strings\": [\"hello\", \"world\"]})\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n        assert response.json() == {\"result\": \"helloworld\"}\n\n        audit_records = in_memory_audit_repo.get_all()\n        assert len(audit_records) == 1\n        assert audit_records[0].source == \"api\"\n        assert audit_records[0].input_count == 2\n        assert audit_records[0].result_length == len(\"helloworld\")\n\n    def test_post_concatenate_empty_list(self, client_no_api_key, in_memory_audit_repo):\n        \"\"\"Tests concatenation of an empty list via the API.\"\"\"\n        response = client_no_api_key.post(\"/concatenate\", json={\"strings\": []})\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n        assert response.json() == {\"result\": \"\"}\n\n        audit_records = in_memory_audit_repo.get_all()\n        assert len(audit_records) == 1\n        assert audit_records[0].input_count == 0\n        assert audit_records[0].result_length == 0\n\n    def test_post_concatenate_invalid_input_type(self, client_no_api_key):\n        \"\"\"Tests API response for invalid input type (e.g., non-list).\"\"\"\n        response = client_no_api_key.post(\"/concatenate\", json={\"strings\": \"not_a_list\"})\n        assert response.status_code == 422 # Pydantic validation error\n\n    def test_post_concatenate_list_with_non_str_elements(self, client_no_api_key):\n        \"\"\"Tests API response for a list containing non-string elements.\"\"\"\n        response = client_no_api_key.post(\"/concatenate\", json={\"strings\": [\"a\", 123, \"b\"]})\n        assert response.status_code == 422 # Pydantic validation error\n\n    def test_post_concatenate_missing_strings_key(self, client_no_api_key):\n        \"\"\"Tests API response when 'strings' key is missing from payload.\"\"\"\n        response = client_no_api_key.post(\"/concatenate\", json={})\n        assert response.status_code == 422 # Pydantic validation error\n\n    def test_api_key_required_and_provided(self, client_with_api_key, in_memory_audit_repo):\n        \"\"\"Tests successful API call when API key is required and provided.\"\"\"\n        headers = {\"X-API-Key\": \"test_api_key\"}\n        response = client_with_api_key.post(\"/concatenate\", json={\"strings\": [\"secure\", \"call\"]}, headers=headers)\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n        assert response.json() == {\"result\": \"securecall\"}\n        assert len(in_memory_audit_repo.get_all()) == 1\n\n    def test_api_key_required_and_missing(self, client_with_api_key):\n        \"\"\"Tests API rejection when API key is required but missing.\"\"\"\n        response = client_with_api_key.post(\"/concatenate\", json={\"strings\": [\"secure\", \"call\"]})\n        assert response.status_code == 401\n        assert response.json() == {\"detail\": \"Invalid or missing API Key\"}\n\n    def test_api_key_required_and_invalid(self, client_with_api_key):\n        \"\"\"Tests API rejection when API key is required but invalid.\"\"\"\n        headers = {\"X-API-Key\": \"wrong_key\"}\n        response = client_with_api_key.post(\"/concatenate\", json={\"strings\": [\"secure\", \"call\"]}, headers=headers)\n        assert response.status_code == 401\n        assert response.json() == {\"detail\": \"Invalid or missing API Key\"}\n\n    def test_api_key_not_required_and_not_provided(self, client_no_api_key):\n        \"\"\"Tests API success when API key is not required and not provided.\"\"\"\n        response = client_no_api_key.post(\"/concatenate\", json={\"strings\": [\"no\", \"key\"]})\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n        assert response.json() == {\"result\": \"nokey\"}\n\n    def test_internal_server_error_handling(self, client_no_api_key, mocker):\n        \"\"\"Tests that an unexpected internal error returns a 500.\"\"\"\n        # Mock Concatenator.concatenate to raise an unexpected exception\n        mocker.patch.object(Concatenator, 'concatenate', side_effect=Exception(\"Internal error\"))\n        response = client_no_api_key.post(\"/concatenate\", json={\"strings\": [\"a\", \"b\"]})\n        assert response.status_code == 500\n        assert response.json() == {\"detail\": \"Internal server error\"}\n```"}
