{"task_id": "HumanEval/37", "solution": "def sort_even(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the odd indicies, while its values at the even indicies are equal\n    to the values of the even indicies of l, but sorted.\n    >>> sort_even([1, 2, 3])\n    [1, 2, 3]\n    >>> sort_even([5, 6, 3, 4])\n    [3, 6, 5, 4]\n    \"\"\"\n    even_values = []\n    even_indices = []\n    for i in range(0, len(l), 2):\n        even_values.append(l[i])\n        even_indices.append(i)\n\n    even_values.sort()\n\n    result = l[:]\n    for i, val in zip(even_indices, even_values):\n        result[i] = val\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/36", "solution": "```\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 requirements.txt\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 .github/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 workflows/\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 ci.yml\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 fizzbuzz_app/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 core.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 utils.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 cli.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 api.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 models.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 exceptions.py\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 __main__.py\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 tests/\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_core.py\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_utils.py\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_cli.py\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_api.py\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_models.py\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 test_exceptions.py\n```\n\n## File Contents\n\n### `pyproject.toml`\n```toml\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"fizzbuzz-app\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"Counts occurrences of digit '7' in numbers divisible by 11 or 13.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nlicense = \"MIT\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"fizzbuzz_app\", from = \"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \">=3.8.1,<4.0\"\nFlask = \"^2.3.2\" # Using a recent Flask version\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^7.0.0\"\nrequests = \"^2.31.0\" # For testing API\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\nfizzbuzz-cli = \"fizzbuzz_app.cli:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n```\n\n### `requirements.txt`\n```\nFlask>=2.3.2\npytest>=7.0.0\nrequests>=2.31.0\n```\n\n### `README.md`\n```markdown\n# FizzBuzz App\n\nThis project provides a Python library, CLI, and HTTP API to count the occurrences of the digit '7' in integers less than `n` that are divisible by 11 or 13.\n\n## Installation\n\nYou can install the library using `pip` or `poetry`:\n\n```bash\n# Using pip\npip install .\n\n# Using poetry\npoetry install\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Library API\n\n```python\nfrom fizzbuzz_app import fizz_buzz, FizzBuzzService\n\n# Using the convenience function\ncount = fizz_buzz(79)\nprint(f\"Count for 79: {count}\") # Output: 3\n\n# Using the service class for custom digits\nservice = FizzBuzzService(digit='3')\ncount_threes = service.count_sevens(35) # Counts '3's in numbers < 35 divisible by 11 or 13\nprint(f\"Count of '3's for 35: {count_threes}\")\n```\n\n### CLI\n\n```bash\n# Using the installed command\nfizzbuzz-cli 79\n# Output: 3\n\n# Using python -m\npython -m fizzbuzz_app 79\n# Output: 3\n```\n\n### HTTP API\n\nThe HTTP API runs on Flask.\n\n```bash\n# To run the development server\n# Make sure you have Flask installed: pip install Flask\nexport FLASK_APP=src/fizzbuzz_app/api.py\nexport FLASK_ENV=development\nflask run\n```\n\nThen, you can make POST requests:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"n\": 79}' http://127.0.0.1:5000/count\n# Expected output: {\"count\": 3}\n```\n```\n\n### `.github/workflows/ci.yml`\n```yaml\nname: CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n  pull_request:\n    branches:\n      - main\n\njobs:\n  build-and-test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        python-version: [\"3.8\", \"3.9\", \"3.10\", \"3.11\"]\n\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    - name: Set up Python ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v4\n      with:\n        python-version: ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n        cache: 'poetry'\n    - name: Install Poetry\n      run: pip install poetry\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: poetry install --no-root\n    - name: Run tests with pytest\n      run: poetry run pytest\n```\n\n### `src/fizzbuzz_app/exceptions.py`\n```python\n\"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input.\"\"\"\n\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input values.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n```\n\n### `src/fizzbuzz_app/models.py`\n```python\n\"\"\"Data Transfer Objects (DTOs) and request/response models.\"\"\"\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\n\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\n@dataclass\nclass CountResult:\n    \"\"\"Represents the result of a digit count operation.\"\"\"\n    count: int\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, int]:\n        \"\"\"Converts the CountResult to a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return {\"count\": self.count}\n\n@dataclass\nclass RequestPayload:\n    \"\"\"Represents the input payload for API requests.\"\"\"\n    n: int\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def from_json(data: Dict[str, Any]) -> 'RequestPayload':\n        \"\"\"Validates and creates a RequestPayload from a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(data, dict):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Request body must be a JSON object.\")\n        \n        n_value = data.get(\"n\")\n        if n_value is None:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Missing 'n' in request payload.\")\n        \n        if not isinstance(n_value, int):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"'n' must be an integer.\")\n        \n        # Additional validation (e.g., non-negative) can be handled by the service layer.\n        return RequestPayload(n=n_value)\n```\n\n### `src/fizzbuzz_app/utils.py`\n```python\n\"\"\"Utility functions for digit counting and input validation.\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Iterable, Any\n\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass DigitUtils:\n    \"\"\"Provides static methods for digit counting and input validation.\"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_DIGIT: str = \"7\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def count_digit_in_number(num: int, digit: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts occurrences of a specific digit in an integer.\"\"\"\n        return str(abs(num)).count(digit)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def count_digit_in_iterable(nums: Iterable[int], digit: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Sums digit occurrences across an iterable of integers.\"\"\"\n        return sum(DigitUtils.count_digit_in_number(n, digit) for n in nums)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def validate_non_negative_int(value: Any) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Validates if a value is a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(value, int):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n        if value < 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer (>= 0).\")\n        return value\n```\n\n### `src/fizzbuzz_app/core.py`\n```python\n\"\"\"Core business logic for counting digits in divisible numbers.\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Iterator, Tuple\n\nfrom .utils import DigitUtils\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass FizzBuzzService:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates the counting of a specific digit in numbers divisible by 11 or 13.\"\"\"\n    DIVISORS: Tuple[int, ...] = (11, 13)\n\n    def __init__(self, digit: str = \"7\", utils: DigitUtils = None):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the service with a target digit and optional DigitUtils instance.\"\"\"\n        self.digit = digit\n        self.utils = utils or DigitUtils()\n\n    def count_sevens(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts digit occurrences in numbers less than n divisible by 11 or 13.\"\"\"\n        validated_n = self.utils.validate_non_negative_int(n)\n        if validated_n == 0:\n            return 0\n        return self._count_digit_in_divisible(validated_n)\n\n    def _iter_divisible(self, n: int) -> Iterator[int]:\n        \"\"\"Yields integers less than n that are divisible by 11 or 13.\"\"\"\n        for i in range(n):\n            for d in self.DIVISORS:\n                if i % d == 0:\n                    yield i\n                    break\n\n    def _count_digit_in_divisible(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Combines divisible number generation and digit counting.\"\"\"\n        return self.utils.count_digit_in_iterable(self._iter_divisible(n), self.digit)\n```\n\n### `src/fizzbuzz_app/__init__.py`\n```python\n\"\"\"Package exports and convenience function.\"\"\"\nfrom .core import FizzBuzzService\nfrom .models import CountResult\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nDEFAULT_DIGIT: str = '7'\n\ndef fizz_buzz(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the number of times the digit 7 appears in integers less than n which are divisible by 11 or 13.\n    >>> fizz_buzz(50)\n    0\n    >>> fizz_buzz(78)\n    2\n    >>> fizz_buzz(79)\n    3\n    \"\"\"\n    service = FizzBuzzService(digit=DEFAULT_DIGIT)\n    return service.count_sevens(n)\n\n__all__ = [\"fizz_buzz\", \"FizzBuzzService\", \"CountResult\", \"InvalidInputError\"]\n```\n\n### `src/fizzbuzz_app/cli.py`\n```python\n\"\"\"Command Line Interface (CLI) for the fizzbuzz_app.\"\"\"\nimport sys\nimport argparse\nfrom typing import List\n\nfrom .core import FizzBuzzService\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass CLIHandler:\n    \"\"\"Handles command-line argument parsing and execution.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: FizzBuzzService = None):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the CLI handler with an optional FizzBuzzService.\"\"\"\n        self.service = service or FizzBuzzService()\n\n    def parse_args(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Parses command-line arguments and returns the integer n.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            description=\"Count '7's in numbers divisible by 11 or 13.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"n\", type=int, help=\"An integer N (count numbers less than N).\"\n        )\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n        return args.n\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Main entry point for the CLI, handling argument parsing and service calls.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            n_value = self.parse_args(argv)\n            count = self.service.count_sevens(n_value)\n            print(count)\n            return 0\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: Invalid input: {e.message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # Use 1 for general errors, 2 for argparse errors (argparse handles its own exit(2))\n        except SystemExit as e:\n            # Argparse raises SystemExit on error or --help\n            return e.code\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the console script.\"\"\"\n    handler = CLIHandler()\n    sys.exit(handler.run(sys.argv[1:]))\n```\n\n### `src/fizzbuzz_app/api.py`\n```python\n\"\"\"HTTP API using Flask for the fizzbuzz_app.\"\"\"\nfrom flask import Flask, request, jsonify, Response\nfrom werkzeug.exceptions import HTTPException\n\nfrom .core import FizzBuzzService\nfrom .models import RequestPayload, CountResult\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass APIHandler:\n    \"\"\"Manages the Flask application and API endpoints.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: FizzBuzzService = None):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the API handler with an optional FizzBuzzService.\"\"\"\n        self.service = service or FizzBuzzService()\n\n    def create_app(self) -> Flask:\n        \"\"\"Creates and configures the Flask application.\"\"\"\n        app = Flask(__name__)\n\n        @app.route(\"/count\", methods=[\"POST\"])\n        def _handle_count() -> Response:\n            \"\"\"Handles the POST /count endpoint.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                payload = RequestPayload.from_json(request.get_json(force=True))\n                result = self.service.count_sevens(payload.n)\n                return jsonify(CountResult(result).to_dict()), 200\n            except InvalidInputError as e:\n                return jsonify({\"error\": e.message}), 400\n            except HTTPException as e:\n                # Catch Flask's internal HTTP errors (e.g., 400 if JSON is malformed)\n                return jsonify({\"error\": str(e.description)}), e.code\n            except Exception:\n                # Catch any other unexpected errors\n                return jsonify({\"error\": \"internal server error\"}), 500\n\n        return app\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    \"\"\"Runs the Flask development server directly.\"\"\"\n    handler = APIHandler()\n    app = handler.create_app()\n    app.run(debug=True, host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=5000)\n```\n\n### `src/fizzbuzz_app/__main__.py`\n```python\n\"\"\"Allows running the CLI as 'python -m fizzbuzz_app'.\"\"\"\nimport sys\nfrom .cli import CLIHandler\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Delegates to CLIHandler for execution.\"\"\"\n    handler = CLIHandler()\n    sys.exit(handler.run(sys.argv[1:]))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n### `tests/test_exceptions.py`\n```python\n\"\"\"Tests for custom exception classes.\"\"\"\nfrom src.fizzbuzz_app.exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\ndef test_invalid_input_error_message():\n    \"\"\"Verify InvalidInputError stores and returns the correct message.\"\"\"\n    message = \"Test error message\"\n    error = InvalidInputError(message)\n    assert str(error) == message\n    assert error.message == message\n```\n\n### `tests/test_models.py`\n```python\n\"\"\"Tests for data models.\"\"\"\nimport pytest\nfrom src.fizzbuzz_app.models import CountResult, RequestPayload\nfrom src.fizzbuzz_app.exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\ndef test_count_result_to_dict():\n    \"\"\"Verify CountResult correctly converts to a dictionary.\"\"\"\n    result = CountResult(count=123)\n    assert result.to_dict() == {\"count\": 123}\n\ndef test_request_payload_from_json_valid_n():\n    \"\"\"Verify RequestPayload handles valid integer 'n' input.\"\"\"\n    data = {\"n\": 100}\n    payload = RequestPayload.from_json(data)\n    assert payload.n == 100\n\ndef test_request_payload_from_json_missing_n():\n    \"\"\"Verify RequestPayload raises error for missing 'n'.\"\"\"\n    data = {\"other_field\": \"value\"}\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"Missing 'n' in request payload.\"):\n        RequestPayload.from_json(data)\n\ndef test_request_payload_from_json_non_integer_n():\n    \"\"\"Verify RequestPayload raises error for non-integer 'n'.\"\"\"\n    data = {\"n\": \"abc\"}\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"'n' must be an integer.\"):\n        RequestPayload.from_json(data)\n\n    data_float = {\"n\": 10.5}\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"'n' must be an integer.\"):\n        RequestPayload.from_json(data_float)\n\ndef test_request_payload_from_json_not_dict():\n    \"\"\"Verify RequestPayload raises error if input is not a dict.\"\"\"\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"Request body must be a JSON object.\"):\n        RequestPayload.from_json(\"not a dict\")\n```\n\n### `tests/test_utils.py`\n```python\n\"\"\"Tests for DigitUtils utility methods.\"\"\"\nimport pytest\nfrom src.fizzbuzz_app.utils import DigitUtils\nfrom src.fizzbuzz_app.exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"num, digit, expected_count\", [\n    (7, \"7\", 1),\n    (17, \"7\", 1),\n    (717, \"7\", 2),\n    (70707, \"7\", 3),\n    (123, \"7\", 0),\n    (0, \"7\", 0),\n    (-7, \"7\", 1), # abs(num) is used\n    (-77, \"7\", 2),\n    (1, \"1\", 1),\n    (10, \"0\", 1),\n])\ndef test_count_digit_in_number(num, digit, expected_count):\n    \"\"\"Test counting a digit in various integer numbers.\"\"\"\n    assert DigitUtils.count_digit_in_number(num, digit) == expected_count\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"nums, digit, expected_total\", [\n    ([7, 17, 717], \"7\", 4),\n    ([1, 2, 3], \"7\", 0),\n    ([], \"7\", 0),\n    ([11, 13, 22, 26], \"1\", 2),\n    ([-7, -17, 0], \"7\", 2),\n])\ndef test_count_digit_in_iterable(nums, digit, expected_total):\n    \"\"\"Test summing digit counts across an iterable.\"\"\"\n    assert DigitUtils.count_digit_in_iterable(nums, digit) == expected_total\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"value, expected_result\", [\n    (10, 10),\n    (0, 0),\n    (10000000, 10000000),\n])\ndef test_validate_non_negative_int_valid_cases(value, expected_result):\n    \"\"\"Verify validate_non_negative_int for valid inputs.\"\"\"\n    assert DigitUtils.validate_non_negative_int(value) == expected_result\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"invalid_value, error_message\", [\n    (\"abc\", \"Input must be an integer.\"),\n    (10.5, \"Input must be an integer.\"),\n    (None, \"Input must be an integer.\"),\n    (-1, \"Input must be a non-negative integer (>= 0).\"),\n    (-100, \"Input must be a non-negative integer (>= 0).\"),\n])\ndef test_validate_non_negative_int_invalid_cases(invalid_value, error_message):\n    \"\"\"Verify validate_non_negative_int raises InvalidInputError for invalid inputs.\"\"\"\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=error_message):\n        DigitUtils.validate_non_negative_int(invalid_value)\n```\n\n### `tests/test_core.py`\n```python\n\"\"\"Tests for the core FizzBuzzService logic and public function.\"\"\"\nimport pytest\nfrom unittest.mock import Mock\n\nfrom src.fizzbuzz_app.core import FizzBuzzService\nfrom src.fizzbuzz_app.exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom src.fizzbuzz_app import fizz_buzz # Test the top-level function\n\n# Mock DigitUtils for isolation\n@pytest.fixture\ndef mock_digit_utils():\n    \"\"\"Provides a mock DigitUtils instance.\"\"\"\n    mock_utils = Mock()\n    mock_utils.validate_non_negative_int.side_effect = lambda n: n # Passthrough for valid ints\n    return mock_utils\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef service(mock_digit_utils):\n    \"\"\"Provides a FizzBuzzService instance with a mocked DigitUtils.\"\"\"\n    return FizzBuzzService(digit=\"7\", utils=mock_digit_utils)\n\ndef test_fizzbuzz_service_init_default_digit():\n    \"\"\"Verify service initializes with default digit.\"\"\"\n    service = FizzBuzzService()