cter group right by one position.\"\"\"\n        # Precondition: len(group) == 3, enforced by service logic.\n        return group[-1] + group[:-1]\n\n```\n\n---\n### `src/cycliccoder/Models.py`\n```python\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nclass EncodeRequest:\n    \"\"\"DTO for an encode operation request.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, input_text: str, persist: bool = False) -> None:\n        self.input_text = input_text\n        self.persist = persist\n\nclass EncodeResponse:\n    \"\"\"DTO for an encode operation response.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, output_text: str) -> None:\n        self.output_text = output_text\n\nclass DecodeRequest:\n    \"\"\"DTO for a decode operation request.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, input_text: str, persist: bool = False) -> None:\n        self.input_text = input_text\n        self.persist = persist\n\nclass DecodeResponse:\n    \"\"\"DTO for a decode operation response.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, output_text: str) -> None:\n        self.output_text = output_text\n\nclass HistoryRecord:\n    \"\"\"DTO for a single history record of an operation.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, input_text: str, output_text: str, operation: str, created_at: str, id: Optional[int] = None) -> None:\n        self.id = id\n        self.input_text = input_text\n        self.output_text = output_text\n        self.operation = operation\n        self.created_at = created_at\n\n```\n\n---\n### `src/cycliccoder/HistoryRepository.py`\n```python\nimport sqlite3\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom cycliccoder.Models import HistoryRecord\nfrom cycliccoder.Exceptions import PersistenceError\n\nDEFAULT_DB_PATH = \"cycliccoder_history.db\"\n\nclass HistoryRepository:\n    \"\"\"Manages persistence of operation history in SQLite.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, db_path: str) -> None:\n        self.db_path = db_path\n        self.conn: sqlite3.Connection = None # type: ignore\n        self._connect()\n        self._ensure_schema()\n\n    def _connect(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Establishes a connection to the SQLite database.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            self.conn = sqlite3.connect(self.db_path)\n            self.conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row # Allows accessing columns by name\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to connect to database at {self.db_path}: {e}\") from e\n\n    def _ensure_schema(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Ensures the necessary table and indexes exist in the database.\"\"\"\n        if not self.conn:\n            raise PersistenceError(\"Database connection not established.\")\n        try:\n            cursor = self.conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS operations (\n                    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n                    input TEXT NOT NULL,\n                    output TEXT NOT NULL,\n                    operation TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(operation IN ('encode','decode')),\n                    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n                )\n            \"\"\")\n            cursor.execute(\"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_operations_operation ON operations(operation)\")\n            cursor.execute(\"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_operations_created_at ON operations(created_at)\")\n            self.conn.commit()\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to ensure database schema: {e}\") from e\n\n    def add(self, record: HistoryRecord) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Inserts a new history record into the database.\"\"\"\n        if not self.conn:\n            raise PersistenceError(\"Database connection not established.\")\n        try:\n            cur = self.conn.cursor()\n            cur.execute(\n                \"INSERT INTO operations (input, output, operation, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n                (record.input_text, record.output_text, record.operation, record.created_at)\n            )\n            self.conn.commit()\n            return cur.lastrowid # type: ignore\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to add record to history: {e}\") from e\n\n    def list_recent(self, limit: int = 50) -> List[HistoryRecord]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a list of the most recent history records.\"\"\"\n        if not self.conn:\n            raise PersistenceError(\"Database connection not established.\")\n        try:\n            cur = self.conn.cursor()\n            cur.execute(\n                \"SELECT id, input, output, operation, created_at FROM operations ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT ?\",\n                (limit,)\n            )\n            rows = cur.fetchall()\n            return [\n                HistoryRecord(\n                    id=row['id'],\n                    input_text=row['input'],\n                    output_text=row['output'],\n                    operation=row['operation'],\n                    created_at=row['created_at']\n                ) for row in rows\n            ]\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to list recent history: {e}\") from e\n\n    def close(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Closes the database connection.\"\"\"\n        if self.conn:\n            self.conn.close()\n            self.conn = None\n\n```\n\n---\n### `src/cycliccoder/EncoderService.py`\n```python\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom cycliccoder.HistoryRepository import HistoryRepository\nfrom cycliccoder.Utils import Utils\nfrom cycliccoder.Models import HistoryRecord\n\nclass EncoderService:\n    \"\"\"Service to encode strings by cyclically shifting groups of three characters.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, repo: Optional[HistoryRepository] = None, utils: Optional[Utils] = None) -> None:\n        self.repo = repo\n        self.utils = utils or Utils()\n\n    def encode(self, s: str, persist: bool = False) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Encodes a string by cycling every complete group of 3 characters left by one position.\n        Partial trailing groups (1 or 2 chars) remain unchanged.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.utils.validate_str(s)\n\n        if not s:\n            return \"\"\n\n        groups = self.utils.group3(s)\n        transformed = []\n        for g in groups:\n            if len(g) == 3:\n                transformed.append(self.utils.left_rotate3(g))\n            else:\n                transformed.append(g)\n        \n        result = \"\".join(transformed)\n\n        if persist and self.repo:\n            record = HistoryRecord(\n                input_text=s,\n                output_text=result,\n                operation=\"encode\",\n                created_at=datetime.utcnow().isoformat()\n            )\n            self.repo.add(record)\n        return result\n\n```\n\n---\n### `src/cycliccoder/DecoderService.py`\n```python\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom cycliccoder.HistoryRepository import HistoryRepository\nfrom cycliccoder.Utils import Utils\nfrom cycliccoder.Models import HistoryRecord\n\nclass DecoderService:\n    \"\"\"Service to decode strings previously encoded by the EncoderService.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, repo: Optional[HistoryRepository] = None, utils: Optional[Utils] = None) -> None:\n        self.repo = repo\n        self.utils = utils or Utils()\n\n    def decode(self, s: str, persist: bool = False) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Decodes a string by reversing the cyclic shift for groups of three characters.\n        Partial trailing groups (1 or 2 chars) remain unchanged.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.utils.validate_str(s)\n\n        if not s:\n            return \"\"\n\n        groups = self.utils.group3(s)\n        transformed = []\n        for g in groups:\n            if len(g) == 3:\n                transformed.append(self.utils.right_rotate3(g))\n            else:\n                transformed.append(g)\n        \n        result = \"\".join(transformed)\n\n        if persist and self.repo:\n            record = HistoryRecord(\n                input_text=s,\n                output_text=result,\n                operation=\"decode\",\n                created_at=datetime.utcnow().isoformat()\n            )\n            self.repo.add(record)\n        return result\n\n```\n\n---\n### `src/cycliccoder/Config.py`\n```python\nclass Config:\n    \"\"\"Runtime configuration holder for cycliccoder.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, db_path: str = \"cycliccoder_history.db\", persist_default: bool = False) -> None:\n        self.db_path = db_path\n        self.persist_default = persist_default\n\n```\n\n---\n### `src/cycliccoder/CLIController.py`\n```python\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom cycliccoder.EncoderService import EncoderService\nfrom cycliccoder.DecoderService import DecoderService\nfrom cycliccoder.HistoryRepository import HistoryRepository\nfrom cycliccoder.Models import HistoryRecord # For type hints\nfrom cycliccoder.Exceptions import InvalidInputError, PersistenceError, CoderError\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles command-line interface argument parsing and dispatches to services.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, encoder: EncoderService, decoder: DecoderService, repo: Optional[HistoryRepository] = None) -> None:\n        self.encoder = encoder\n        self.decoder = decoder\n        self.repo = repo\n        self._parser = self._setup_parser()\n\n    def _setup_parser(self) -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n        \"\"\"Configures the argparse parser for the CLI.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"cycliccoder-cli\",\n            description=\"Encode and decode strings by cycling groups of three characters.\"\n        )\n\n        subparsers = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", help=\"Available commands\")\n\n        # Encode subcommand\n        encode_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\"encode\", help=\"Encode a string\")\n        encode_parser.add_argument(\"text\", type=str, help=\"The string to encode\")\n        encode_parser.add_argument(\n            \"--persist\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"Persist the operation to history.\"\n        )\n        encode_parser.set_defaults(func=self._cmd_encode)\n\n        # Decode subcommand\n        decode_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\"decode\", help=\"Decode a string\")\n        decode_parser.add_argument(\"text\", type=str, help=\"The string to decode\")\n        decode_parser.add_argument(\n            \"--persist\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"Persist the operation to history.\"\n        )\n        decode_parser.set_defaults(func=self._cmd_decode)\n\n        # History subcommand\n        history_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\"history\", help=\"View recent operation history\")\n        history_parser.add_argument(\n            \"--limit\",\n            type=int,\n            default=10,\n            help=\"Number of recent operations to display (default: 10).\"\n        )\n        history_parser.set_defaults(func=self._cmd_history)\n\n        return parser\n\n    def handle(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Parses arguments and executes the corresponding command.\"\"\"\n        args = self._parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n        if not hasattr(args, \"func\"):\n            self._parser.print_help()\n            return 1\n\n        try:\n            return args.func(args)\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        except PersistenceError as e:\n            print(f\"Persistence Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        except CoderError as e:\n            print(f\"Application Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\n    def _cmd_encode(self, args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Executes the encode command.\"\"\"\n        result = self.encoder.encode(args.text, persist=args.persist)\n        print(result)\n        return 0\n\n    def _cmd_decode(self, args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Executes the decode command.\"\"\"\n        result = self.decoder.decode(args.text, persist=args.persist)\n        print(result)\n        return 0\n\n    def _cmd_history(self, args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Executes the history command.\"\"\"\n        if not self.repo:\n            print(\"Error: History persistence is not configured.\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        \n        records = self.repo.list_recent(limit=args.limit)\n        \n        if not records:\n            print(\"No history records found.\")\n            return 0\n\n        # Simple table formatting\n        headers = [\"ID\", \"Operation\", \"Input\", \"Output\", \"Timestamp\"]\n        print(f\"{headers[0]:<5} {headers[1]:<10} {headers[2]:<25} {headers[3]:<25} {headers[4]}\")\n        print(\"-\" * 90) # Adjust width as needed\n        \n        for r in records:\n            input_preview = (r.input_text[:22] + '...') if len(r.input_text) > 25 else r.input_text\n            output_preview = (r.output_text[:22] + '...') if len(r.output_text) > 25 else r.output_text\n            print(f\"{r.id:<5} {r.operation:<10} {input_preview:<25} {output_preview:<25} {r.created_at}\")\n        return 0\n\n```\n\n---\n### `src/cycliccoder/App.py`\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom cycliccoder.Config import Config\nfrom cycliccoder.HistoryRepository import HistoryRepository\nfrom cycliccoder.EncoderService import EncoderService\nfrom cycliccoder.DecoderService import DecoderService\nfrom cycliccoder.CLIController import CLIController\nfrom cycliccoder.Exceptions import CoderError, PersistenceError\n\nclass App:\n    \"\"\"The main application class, responsible for wiring dependencies and running the CLI.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, config: Optional[Config] = None, repo: Optional[HistoryRepository] = None) -> None:\n        self.config = config or Config()\n        \n        # If repo is not provided, create a default one based on config\n        self.repo = repo if repo is not None else HistoryRepository(self.config.db_path)\n        \n        self.encoder = EncoderService(repo=self.repo)\n        self.decoder = DecoderService(repo=self.repo)\n        self.cli_controller = CLIController(encoder=self.encoder, decoder=self.decoder, repo=self.repo)\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Runs the application, typically by dispatching to the CLI controller.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            return self.cli_controller.handle(argv)\n        except PersistenceError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: Database persistence issue: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        except CoderError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: An application error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Error: An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        finally:\n            # Ensure repository connection is closed when app exits\n            if self.repo:\n                self.repo.close()\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    \"\"\"Main function to instantiate and run the App.\"\"\"\n    app = App()\n    return app.run(sys.argv[1:])\n\n```\n\n---\n### `src/cycliccoder/__init__.py`\n```python\n\"\"\"\nA small, reusable library and CLI to encode and decode strings by cycling groups of three characters.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .App import App, main\nfrom .Config import Config\nfrom .Models import (\n    EncodeRequest, EncodeResponse,\n    DecodeRequest, DecodeResponse,\n    HistoryRecord\n)\nfrom .EncoderService import EncoderService\nfrom .DecoderService import DecoderService\nfrom .HistoryRepository import HistoryRepository, DEFAULT_DB_PATH\nfrom .CLIController import CLIController\nfrom .Utils import Utils\nfrom .Exceptions import CoderError, InvalidInputError, PersistenceError\n\n# Expose main entry point for scripts\n__all__ = [\n    \"App\", \"main\", \"Config\",\n    \"EncodeRequest\", \"EncodeResponse\",\n    \"DecodeRequest\", \"DecodeResponse\",\n    \"HistoryRecord\",\n    \"EncoderService\", \"DecoderService\",\n    \"HistoryRepository\", \"DEFAULT_DB_PATH\",\n    \"CLIController\",\n    \"Utils\",\n    \"CoderError\", \"InvalidInputError\", \"PersistenceError\",\n]\n\n```\n\n---\n### `pyproject.toml`\n```toml\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"cycliccoder\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A small library and CLI to encode/decode strings by cycling groups of three characters.\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.9\"\nlicense = { file = \"LICENSE\" } # Assuming a LICENSE file exists\nkeywords = [\"encoding\", \"decoding\", \"cli\", \"library\"]\nauthors = [\n  { name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" }, # Placeholder\n]\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\", # Assuming MIT License\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n    \"Intended Audience :: Developers\",\n    \"Topic :: Software Development :: Libraries :: Python Modules\",\n    \"Topic :: Text Processing\",\n]\ndependencies = [\n    # No external dependencies for runtime, only stdlib\n]\n\n[project.urls]\nHomepage = \"https://github.com/yourusername/cyclic-coder\" # Replace with actual repo\n\"Bug Tracker\" = \"https://github.com/yourusername/cyclic-coder/issues\" # Replace\n\n[project.scripts]\ncycliccoder-cli = \"cycliccoder.App:main\" # This defines the CLI entry point\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\ndev = [\n    \"pytest>=7.0\",\n    \"flake8>=6.0\",\n    \"mypy>=1.0\",\n]\n\n```\n\n---\n### `README.md`\n```markdown\n# Cyclic Coder\n\nA small Python library and CLI to encode and decode strings by cyclically shifting groups of three characters.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Encode/Decode API**: Programmatic functions to transform strings.\n- **CLI Tool**: A command-line interface for easy encoding, decoding, and history lookup.\n- **Operation History**: Persists all encode/decode operations (input, output, type, timestamp) to a local SQLite database for auditability and repeatability.\n- **No External Dependencies**: Built entirely using Python's standard library.\n- **Modular Design**: Separated into services, repository, controllers, and utilities for testability and maintainability.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\n# Clone the repository\ngit clone https://github.com/yourusername/cyclic-coder.git # Replace with actual repo URL\ncd cyclic-coder\n\n# Install in editable mode for development (includes dev dependencies)\npip install -e .[dev]\n\n# Or, install as a regular package\npip install .\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Command Line Interface (CLI)\n\nThe `cycliccoder-cli` command is installed upon package installation.\n\n**1. Encode a string:**\n\n```bash\ncycliccoder-cli encode \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\"\n# Output: bcaefdghi jklmno pqrstu vwxyz\n```\n\nTo persist the operation to the history database:\n\n```bash\ncycliccoder-cli encode \"mysecrettext\" --persist\n# Output: ysecretmxtte\n```\n\n**2. Decode a string:**\n\n```bash\ncycliccoder-cli decode \"bcaefdghi jklmno pqrstu vwxyz\"\n# Output: abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\n```\n\nTo persist the decode operation:\n\n```bash\ncycliccoder-cli decode \"ysecretmxtte\" --persist\n# Output: mysecrettext\n```\n\n**3. View history:**\n\n```bash\ncycliccoder-cli history\n# Displays a table of the 10 most recent operations.\n\ncycliccoder-cli history --limit 5\n# Displays the 5 most recent operations.\n```\n\n### Library API\n\nYou can import and use the `EncoderService` and `DecoderService` classes in your Python applications.\n\n```python\nfrom cycliccoder import EncoderService, DecoderService, HistoryRepository, Config\n\n# Initialize configuration (optional, defaults are usually fine)\nconfig = Config(db_path=\"my_custom_history.db\")\n\n# Initialize the history repository (optional, can pass None to services if no persistence)\nrepo = HistoryRepository(db_path=config.db_path)\n\n# Initialize services\nencoder = EncoderService(repo=repo)\ndecoder = DecoderService(repo=repo)\n\n# Encode a string\noriginal_text = \"HelloPython\"\nencoded_text = encoder.encode(original_text, persist=True)\nprint(f\"Original: {original_text}\")\nprint(f\"Encoded: {encoded_text}\")\n# Expected: Original: HelloPython, Encoded: eloHhPyton\n\n# Decode a string\ndecoded_text = decoder.decode(encoded_text, persist=True)\nprint(f\"Decoded: {decoded_text}\")\n# Expected: Decoded: HelloPython\n\n# Query history\nrecent_operations = repo.list_recent(limit=3)\nfor op in recent_operations:\n    print(f\"[{op.created_at}] {op.operation}: '{op.input_text}' -> '{op.output_text}'\")\n\n# Remember to close the repository connection when done\nrepo.close()\n```\n\n## Development\n\n### Running Tests\n\nTo run unit tests, ensure you have `pytest` installed (included in `dev` dependencies):\n\n```bash\npytest\n```\n\n### Type Checking and Linting\n\n```bash\nflake8 src/\nmypy src/\n```\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 cycliccoder/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py         # Package initialization and exports\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 App.py              # Application wiring, entrypoint\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 Config.py           # Runtime configuration\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 Models.py           # Data Transfer Objects (DTOs) and HistoryRecord\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 EncoderService.py   # Core encoding logic\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 DecoderService.py   # Core decoding logic\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 HistoryRepository.py# SQLite persistence for history\n\u2502      