{"task_id": "HumanEval/48", "solution": "```python\n# pyproject.toml\n# This file defines project metadata, dependencies, and entry points.\n# It uses PEP 621 format for project definition.\n\"\"\"\n[project]\nname = \"palindrome-checker\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A reusable Python library and service to check whether a string is a palindrome.\"\nauthors = [{ name = \"AI Assistant\", email = \"ai@example.com\" }]\ndependencies = [\n    \"fastapi>=0.111.0\",\n    \"uvicorn>=0.29.0\",\n    \"pydantic>=2.0\",\n]\nrequires-python = \">=3.9\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nlicense = { text = \"MIT\" }\n\n[project.scripts]\npalcheck = \"palindrome_checker.controllers.CLIController:main\"\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\ndev = [\n    \"pytest>=8.0\",\n    \"coverage>=7.0\",\n    \"httpx>=0.27.0\"\n]\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\"\"\"\n\n# README.md\n# Provides a general overview, installation instructions, and usage examples.\n\"\"\"\n# Palindrome Checker\n\nThis project provides a reusable Python library and small service to check whether a string is a palindrome. It includes options for normalization, persistent history, and exposes both a command-line interface (CLI) and a minimal HTTP API.\n\n## Features\n\n-   **Core Library**: A `PalindromeChecker` class to determine if a string is a palindrome with various normalization options.\n-   **Normalization**: Supports case folding, removing non-alphanumeric characters, and Unicode NFKC normalization.\n-   **Pluggable Persistence**: Stores check history (input, normalized value, result, timestamp) with adapters for in-memory (for testing) and SQLite (for production).\n-   **CLI**: A `palcheck` command for quick checks.\n-   **HTTP API**: A `/check` endpoint for programmatic integration.\n-   **Well-tested**: Designed for testability with dependency injection.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\n# Clone the repository\ngit clone <repository-url>\ncd palindrome-checker\n\n# Ensure Poetry is installed (pip install poetry)\npoetry install --with dev\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### CLI\n\nTo check a string:\n```bash\npalcheck \"A man, a plan, a canal: Panama\"\n# Example output:\n# Input: \"A man, a plan, a canal: Panama\"\n# Normalized: \"amanaplanacanalpanama\"\n# Is Palindrome: True\n# Checked At: 2023-10-27T10:00:00.123456+00:00 (example timestamp)\n```\n\nTo disable normalization:\n```bash\npalcheck \"Racecar\" --no-normalize\n```\n\nTo disable saving history:\n```bash\npalcheck \"level\" --no-save\n```\n\nTo get JSON output:\n```bash\npalcheck \"madam\" --json\n```\n\n### HTTP API\n\n1.  **Run the server**:\n    ```bash\n    python scripts/run_server.py\n    ```\n    The server will typically run on `http://127.0.0.1:8000`.\n\n2.  **Make a POST request**:\n    ```bash\n    curl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n         -d '{\"text\": \"No lemon, no melon\", \"normalize\": true}' \\\n         http://127.0.0.1:8000/check\n    ```\n    Expected JSON response:\n    ```json\n    {\n      \"input_text\": \"No lemon, no melon\",\n      \"normalized_text\": \"nolemonnomelon\",\n      \"is_palindrome\": true,\n      \"checked_at\": \"2023-10-27T10:00:00.123456+00:00\"\n    }\n    ```\n\n## Configuration\n\nThe application can be configured via environment variables or by passing a `Config` object to the `PalindromeChecker` constructor.\n\n-   `PALINDROME_CHECKER_DB_URL`: SQLite database URL (e.g., `sqlite:///./history.db`).\n-   `PALINDROME_CHECKER_NORMALIZE_BY_DEFAULT`: `true` or `false` to control default normalization.\n\n## Development\n\nRun tests:\n```bash\npoetry run pytest\n```\n\n## CI/CD\n\nA GitHub Actions workflow (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) is provided for continuous integration.\n\"\"\"\n\n# scripts/run_server.py\n# This script provides a simple way to run the FastAPI HTTP server.\n\"\"\"\nimport uvicorn\nfrom palindrome_checker.controllers.HTTPController import create_http_app\nfrom palindrome_checker.Logger import get_logger\n\nlogger = get_logger(__name__)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    app = create_http_app() # Encapsulates dependency injection setup\n    logger.info(\"Starting HTTP server...\")\n    uvicorn.run(app, host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=8000)\n\"\"\"\n\n# .github/workflows/ci.yml\n# GitHub Actions workflow for continuous integration.\n# It sets up Python, installs dependencies, runs tests, and reports coverage.\n\"\"\"\nname: CI/CD Pipeline\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n      - develop\n  pull_request:\n    branches:\n      - main\n      - develop\n\njobs:\n  build-and-test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n\n    steps:\n    - name: Checkout code\n      uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n    - name: Set up Python\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n      with:\n        python-version: '3.9' \n        cache: 'poetry' # Use poetry for dependency caching\n\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: |\n        pip install poetry\n        poetry install --with dev\n\n    - name: Run tests with pytest\n      run: |\n        poetry run pytest --cov=src/palindrome_checker --cov-report=xml\n      env:\n        # Use in-memory DB for tests to ensure isolated and fast execution\n        PALINDROME_CHECKER_DB_URL: sqlite:///:memory: \n\n    - name: Upload coverage report\n      uses: codecov/codecov-action@v4\n      with:\n        files: ./coverage.xml\n        fail_ci_if_error: true\n\"\"\"\n\n# src/palindrome_checker/__init__.py\n# Package initializer, exposing key modules and a dependency setup function.\n\"\"\"\nfrom .Config import Config\nfrom .Models import PalindromeCheckRequest, PalindromeCheckResult, HistoryRecord\nfrom .Exceptions import PalindromeError, InvalidInputError, RepositoryError\nfrom .Utils import current_utc_iso, is_string, safe_reverse\nfrom .Normalizer import Normalizer\nfrom .HistoryRepository import HistoryRepository\nfrom .InMemoryHistoryRepository import InMemoryHistoryRepository\nfrom .SQLiteHistoryRepository import SQLiteHistoryRepository\nfrom .PalindromeChecker import PalindromeChecker\nfrom .Logger import get_logger\n\n# Define a function for easy dependency injection setup for internal use\ndef setup_dependencies(config: Config = None) -> PalindromeChecker:\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    Sets up and returns a PalindromeChecker instance with its dependencies.\n    Uses default configuration or provided config, and a SQLite repository.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    if config is None:\n        config = Config() # Load default or from env\n\n    normalizer = Normalizer()\n    repository = SQLiteHistoryRepository(db_path=config.db_url.replace(\"sqlite:///\", \"\"))\n    checker = PalindromeChecker(normalizer=normalizer, repository=repository, config=config)\n    return checker\n\"\"\"\n\n# src/palindrome_checker/Logger.py\n# Provides a standardized logging configuration for the application.\n\"\"\"\nimport logging\nimport os\n\ndef get_logger(name: str = \"palindrome_checker\") -> logging.Logger:\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    Configures and returns a logger for the application.\n    Logs to console with INFO level by default, configurable via LOG_LEVEL.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    logger = logging.getLogger(name)\n    if not logger.handlers: # Prevent adding multiple handlers if called multiple times\n        handler = logging.StreamHandler()\n        formatter = logging.Formatter('%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n        handler.setFormatter(formatter)\n        logger.addHandler(handler)\n        logger.setLevel(os.environ.get(\"LOG_LEVEL\", \"INFO\").upper())\n    return logger\n\"\"\"\n\n# src/palindrome_checker/Config.py\n# Dataclass to hold application configuration, with environment variable support.\n\"\"\"\nimport os\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Config:\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    Configuration dataclass for the application.\n    Fields are immutable after initialization.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    db_url: str\n    normalize_by_default: bool\n\n    def __init__(self, db_url: str = None, normalize_by_default: bool = None) -> None:\n        # Use object.__setattr__ for frozen dataclasses\n        object.__setattr__(self, 'db_url', db_url if db_url is not None else os.environ.get(\"PALINDROME_CHECKER_DB_URL\", \"sqlite:///./palindrome_history.db\"))\n        \n        default_normalize_env = os.environ.get(\"PALINDROME_CHECKER_NORMALIZE_BY_DEFAULT\")\n        if normalize_by_default is not None:\n            object.__setattr__(self, 'normalize_by_default', normalize_by_default)\n        elif default_normalize_env is not None:\n            object.__setattr__(self, 'normalize_by_default', default_normalize_env.lower() == 'true')\n        else:\n            object.__setattr__(self, 'normalize_by_default', True) # Default to True as per spec\n\"\"\"\n\n# src/palindrome_checker/Models.py\n# Defines Data Transfer Objects (DTOs) and domain models using dataclasses.\n\"\"\"\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict, Any\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel # For FastAPI compatibility\n\nclass PalindromeCheckRequest(BaseModel):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    Pydantic model for incoming palindrome check requests via HTTP API.\n    Used for request body validation and deserialization.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    text: str\n    normalize: Optional[bool] = None\n    save: bool = True\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass PalindromeCheckResult:\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    DTO for the result of a palindrome check.\n    Includes input, normalized text, and the outcome.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    input_text: str\n    normalized_text: str\n    is_palindrome: bool\n    checked_at: str # ISO-8601 UTC timestamp\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Converts the result to a dictionary, suitable for JSON serialization.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n        return {\n            \"input_text\": self.input_text,\n            \"normalized_text\": self.normalized_text,\n            \"is_palindrome\": self.is_palindrome,\n            \"checked_at\": self.checked_at,\n        }\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass HistoryRecord:\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    Data model for persisting palindrome check history.\n    Includes a unique ID for storage.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    id: Optional[int]\n    input_text: str\n    normalized_text: str\n    is_palindrome: bool\n    checked_at: str\n\"\"\"\n\n# src/palindrome_checker/Exceptions.py\n# Defines custom exception classes specific to the palindrome checker domain.\n\"\"\"\nclass PalindromeError(Exception):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Base exception for palindrome checker domain errors.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    pass\n\nclass InvalidInputError(PalindromeError):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Raised when input validation fails (e.g., non-string, empty if disallowed).\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n\nclass RepositoryError(PalindromeError):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Raised when a persistence operation fails.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n\"\"\"\n\n# src/palindrome_checker/Utils.py\n# Provides small, generic utility functions.\n\"\"\"\nimport datetime\nimport unicodedata\nimport re\nfrom typing import Any\n\ndef current_utc_iso() -> str:\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Returns the current UTC time as an ISO-8601 formatted string.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    return datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec='microseconds')\n\ndef is_string(obj: Any) -> bool:\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Checks if the given object is an instance of str.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    return isinstance(obj, str)\n\ndef safe_reverse(s: str) -> str:\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Reverses a string. Useful for palindrome checks and handling empty strings.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    return s[::-1]\n\"\"\"\n\n# src/palindrome_checker/Normalizer.py\n# Implements the string normalization logic using configurable steps.\n\"\"\"\nimport unicodedata\nimport re\nfrom palindrome_checker.Exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom palindrome_checker.Utils import is_string\n\nclass Normalizer:\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    Handles various text normalization strategies for palindrome checking.\n    Applies Unicode normalization, case folding, and non-alphanumeric removal.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    def __init__(self, remove_non_alnum: bool = True, case_fold: bool = True, unicode_form: str = \"NFKC\") -> None:\n        self.remove_non_alnum = remove_non_alnum\n        self.case_fold = case_fold\n        self.unicode_form = unicode_form\n\n    def normalize(self, text: str) -> str:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\n        Applies configured normalization steps to the input text.\n        Steps: Unicode normalization, case folding, non-alphanumeric removal.\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\n        if not is_string(text):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input for normalization must be a string.\")\n        \n        s = text\n        # 1. Unicode normalization (e.g., for compatibility decomposition)\n        if self.unicode_form:\n            s = unicodedata.normalize(self.unicode_form, s)\n        \n        # 2. Case folding (more aggressive than .lower() for Unicode)\n        if self.case_fold:\n            s = s.casefold()\n        \n        # 3. Remove non-alphanumeric characters (including non-letters/numbers)\n        # Using \\p{L} for Unicode letters, and \\d for digits\n        if self.remove_non_alnum:\n            s = re.sub(r'[^\\p{L}\\d]', '', s, flags=re.UNICODE)\n        \n        return s\n\"\"\"\n\n# src/palindrome_checker/HistoryRepository.py\n# Defines the abstract interface for history persistence.\n\"\"\"\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom typing import List\nfrom palindrome_checker.Models import HistoryRecord\n\nclass HistoryRepository(ABC):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    Abstract Base Class for palindrome check history repositories.\n    Defines the contract for saving and querying history records.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    @abstractmethod\n    def save(self, record: HistoryRecord) -> None:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Saves a HistoryRecord to the repository.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def query_recent(self, limit: int = 100) -> List[HistoryRecord]:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Queries the N most recent HistoryRecords, ordered from newest to oldest.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n        pass\n\"\"\"\n\n# src/palindrome_checker/InMemoryHistoryRepository.py\n# An in-memory implementation of HistoryRepository, suitable for testing.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom palindrome_checker.HistoryRepository import HistoryRepository\nfrom palindrome_checker.Models import HistoryRecord\n\nclass InMemoryHistoryRepository(HistoryRepository):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    An in-memory implementation of HistoryRepository, primarily for testing.\n    Records are stored in a list and are not persistent across application runs.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        self._store: List[HistoryRecord] = []\n        self._next_id: int = 1\n\n    def save(self, record: HistoryRecord) -> None:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\n        Saves a HistoryRecord to the in-memory store.\n        Assigns an incremental ID if not already present, ensuring immutability.\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\n        if record.id is None:\n            # Create a new record with an assigned ID for immutability\n            new_record = HistoryRecord(\n                id=self._next_id,\n                input_text=record.input_text,\n                normalized_text=record.normalized_text,\n                is_palindrome=record.is_palindrome,\n                checked_at=record.checked_at\n            )\n            self._store.append(new_record)\n            self._next_id += 1\n        else:\n            # If an ID is provided, assume it's for an existing record\n            # For simplicity, this in-memory repo just appends.\n            # A real repo would update or ensure uniqueness.\n            self._store.append(record)\n\n    def all(self) -> List[HistoryRecord]:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Returns all stored HistoryRecords.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n        return list(self._store)\n\n    def query_recent(self, limit: int = 100) -> List[HistoryRecord]:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Returns the most recent N HistoryRecords from the store (newest first).\\\"\\\"\\\"\n        # For a simple list, 'recent' means the end of the list, then reversed.\n        return self._store[-limit:][::-1]\n\"\"\"\n\n# src/palindrome_checker/SQLiteHistoryRepository.py\n# SQLite implementation for persistent history storage.\n\"\"\"\nimport sqlite3\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom palindrome_checker.HistoryRepository import HistoryRepository\nfrom palindrome_checker.Models import HistoryRecord\nfrom palindrome_checker.Exceptions import RepositoryError\nfrom palindrome_checker.Logger import get_logger\n\nlogger = get_logger(__name__)\n\n# SQL statement to create the history table if it does not exist.\nCREATE_TABLE_SQL = \\\"\\\"\\\"\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS history (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    input_text TEXT NOT NULL,\n    normalized_text TEXT NOT NULL,\n    is_palindrome INTEGER NOT NULL,\n    checked_at TEXT NOT NULL\n)\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\n# SQL statement to create an index for efficient querying by timestamp.\nCREATE_INDEX_SQL = \"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_history_checked_at ON history(checked_at DESC)\"\n\nclass SQLiteHistoryRepository(HistoryRepository):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    SQLite implementation of HistoryRepository.\n    Persists palindrome check history to a specified SQLite database file.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    def __init__(self, db_path: str) -> None:\n        self.db_path = db_path\n        self._ensure_schema()\n\n    def _connect(self) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Establishes a connection to the SQLite database.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n        try:\n            conn = sqlite3.connect(self.db_path)\n            conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row # Allows accessing columns by name\n            return conn\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Failed to connect to SQLite database at {self.db_path}: {e}\")\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Database connection failed: {e}\")\n\n    def _ensure_schema(self) -> None:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Ensures the 'history' table and necessary indexes exist in the database.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n        try:\n            with self._connect() as conn:\n                cursor = conn.cursor()\n                cursor.execute(CREATE_TABLE_SQL)\n                cursor.execute(CREATE_INDEX_SQL)\n                conn.commit()\n                logger.info(f\"SQLite schema ensured for {self.db_path}\")\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            logger.critical(f\"Failed to ensure SQLite schema for {self.db_path}: {e}\")\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Schema initialization failed: {e}\")\n\n    def save(self, record: HistoryRecord) -> None:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Saves a HistoryRecord to the SQLite database.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n        try:\n            with self._connect() as conn:\n                cursor = conn.cursor()\n                cursor.execute(\n                    \"INSERT INTO history (input_text, normalized_text, is_palindrome, checked_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n                    (record.input_text, record.normalized_text, int(record.is_palindrome), record.checked_at)\n                )\n                conn.commit()\n                # Update the record ID if it was inserted, for consistency with in-memory repo\n                object.__setattr__(record, 'id', cursor.lastrowid) # Safely set ID on frozen dataclass\n                logger.debug(f\"Saved record with ID {record.id}\")\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Failed to save record to SQLite: {e}\")\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Failed to save record: {e}\")\n\n    def query_recent(self, limit: int = 100) -> List[HistoryRecord]:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Queries the N most recent HistoryRecords from the SQLite database (newest first).\\\"\\\"\\\"\n        try:\n            with self._connect() as conn:\n                cursor = conn.cursor()\n                cursor.execute(\n                    \"SELECT id, input_text, normalized_text, is_palindrome, checked_at FROM history ORDER BY checked_at DESC LIMIT ?\",\n                    (limit,)\n                )\n                rows = cursor.fetchall()\n                return [\n                    HistoryRecord(\n                        id=row['id'],\n                        input_text=row['input_text'],\n                        normalized_text=row['normalized_text'],\n                        is_palindrome=bool(row['is_palindrome']),\n                        checked_at=row['checked_at']\n                    ) for row in rows\n                ]\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Failed to query recent records from SQLite: {e}\")\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Failed to query records: {e}\")\n\"\"\"\n\n# src/palindrome_checker/PalindromeChecker.py\n# The core service class that orchestrates palindrome checking and persistence.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom palindrome_checker.Normalizer import Normalizer\nfrom palindrome_checker.HistoryRepository import HistoryRepository\nfrom palindrome_checker.Config import Config\nfrom palindrome_checker.Models import PalindromeCheckResult, HistoryRecord\nfrom palindrome_checker.Exceptions import InvalidInputError, RepositoryError\nfrom palindrome_checker.Utils import current_utc_iso, is_string, safe_reverse\nfrom palindrome_checker.Logger import get_logger\n\nlogger = get_logger(__name__)\n\nclass PalindromeChecker:\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    Core service for checking if a string is a palindrome.\n    Orchestrates normalization, palindrome logic, and history persistence.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    def __init__(self, normalizer: Normalizer, repository: HistoryRepository, config: Config) -> None:\n        self.normalizer = normalizer\n        self.repository = repository\n        self.config = config\n\n    def is_palindrome(self, text: str, normalize: Optional[bool] = None, save: bool = True) -> PalindromeCheckResult:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\n        Checks if the given text is a palindrome, with options for normalization and history saving.\n        Returns a PalindromeCheckResult object containing details of the check.\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\n        if not is_string(text):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'text' must be a string.\")\n        \n        # Determine whether to normalize based on the 'normalize' argument or default config\n        effective_normalize = normalize if normalize is not None else self.config.normalize_by_default\n\n        normalized_text = self.normalizer.normalize(text) if effective_normalize else text\n        \n        # Perform the palindrome check. An empty string is considered a palindrome by default.\n        is_pal = safe_reverse(normalized_text) == normalized_text\n\n        checked_at = current_utc_iso()\n        \n        result = PalindromeCheckResult(\n            input_text=text,\n            normalized_text=normalized_text,\n            is_palindrome=is_pal,\n            checked_at=checked_at\n        )\n\n        if save:\n            try:\n                rec = HistoryRecord(\n                    id=None, # ID will be assigned by the repository\n                    input_text=text,\n                    normalized_text=normalized_text,\n                    is_palindrome=is_pal,\n                    checked_at=checked_at\n                )\n                self.repository.save(rec)\n            except RepositoryError as e:\n                logger.error(f\"Failed to save palindrome check history: {e}\")\n                # As per spec, log error and re-raise RepositoryError\n                raise e\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.critical(f\"An unexpected error occurred while saving history: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n                raise RepositoryError(f\"Unexpected error during history save: {e}\") from e\n\n        return result\n\"\"\"\n\n# src/palindrome_checker/controllers/CLIController.py\n# Handles command-line interface interactions.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nimport json\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom palindrome_checker.PalindromeChecker import PalindromeChecker\nfrom palindrome_checker.Exceptions import InvalidInputError, RepositoryError\nfrom palindrome_checker.Logger import get_logger\nfrom palindrome_checker.Config import Config\nfrom palindrome_checker.SQLiteHistoryRepository import SQLiteHistoryRepository\nfrom palindrome_checker.Normalizer import Normalizer\n\nlogger = get_logger(__name__)\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    Handles command-line interface interactions for the palindrome checker.\n    Parses arguments, calls the core service, and prints results.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    def __init__(self, checker: PalindromeChecker, logger_instance=None) -> None:\n        self.checker = checker\n        self.logger = logger_instance if logger_instance else get_logger(__name__)\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\n        Parses CLI arguments and executes the palindrome check.\n        Returns an exit code (0 for success, non-zero for errors).\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"palcheck\",\n            description=\"Checks if a string is a palindrome with normalization and history options.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"text\",\n            type=str,\n            help=\"The string to check for palindrome property.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--no-normalize\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"Disable normalization (case folding, removing non-alphanumeric).\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--no-save\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"Do not save the check result to history.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--json\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"Output the result in JSON format.\"\n        )\n\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv[1:])\n\n        try:\n            result = self.checker.is_palindrome(\n                text=args.text,\n                normalize=not args.no_normalize,\n                save=not args.no_save\n            )\n\n            if args.json:\n                print(json.dumps(result.to_dict(), indent=2))\n            else:\n                print(f\"Input: {result.input_text!r}\")\n                print(f\"Normalized: {result.normalized_text!r}\")\n                print(f\"Is Palindrome: {result.is_palindrome}\")\n                print(f\"Checked At: {result.checked_at}\")\n            return 0\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            self.logger.error(f\"Invalid input: {e}\")\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2 # Exit code 2 for invalid input\n        except RepositoryError as e:\n            self.logger.error(f\"Persistence error: {e}\")\n            print(f\"Error: A database error occurred while saving history. {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 3 # Exit code 3 for persistence error\n        except Exception as e:\n            self.logger.critical(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # Generic error code\n\ndef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    Entry point for the CLI command.\n    Sets up dependencies and runs the CLI controller.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    if argv is None:\n        argv = sys.argv\n    \n    # Dependency Injection setup for CLI\n    config = Config() # Loads from env or uses defaults\n    normalizer = Normalizer()\n    repository = SQLiteHistoryRepository(db_path=config.db_url.replace(\"sqlite:///\", \"\"))\n    checker = PalindromeChecker(normalizer=normalizer, repository=repository, config=config)\n    \n    controller = CLIController(checker=checker)\n    return controller.run(argv)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n\"\"\"\n\n# src/palindrome_checker/controllers/HTTPController.py\n# Implements the FastAPI HTTP API endpoints.\n\"\"\"\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, status\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict, Any\nfrom palindrome_checker.PalindromeChecker import PalindromeChecker\nfrom palindrome_checker.Models import PalindromeCheckRequest, PalindromeCheckResult\nfrom palindrome_checker.Exceptions import InvalidInputError, RepositoryError\nfrom palindrome_checker.Logger import get_logger\nfrom palindrome_checker.Config import Config\nfrom palindrome_checker.SQLiteHistoryRepository import SQLiteHistoryRepository\nfrom palindrome_checker.Normalizer import Normalizer\n\nlogger = get_logger(__name__)\n\nclass HTTPController:\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    FastAPI controller for the palindrome checking service.\n    Exposes an HTTP endpoint to perform checks and returns structured responses.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    def __init__(self, checker: PalindromeChecker) -> None:\n        self.checker = checker\n        self.app = FastAPI(\n            title=\"Palindrome Checker API\",\n            description=\"API to check if a string is a palindrome with normalization and history.\",\n            version=\"0.1.0\"\n        )\n        self.register_routes()\n\n    def register_routes(self) -> None:\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Registers the API routes with the FastAPI application.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n\n        @self.app.post(\"/check\", response_model=PalindromeCheckResult, status_code=status.HTTP_200_OK)\n        async def check(request: PalindromeCheckRequest) -> PalindromeCheckResult:\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"\n            Endpoint to check if a given string is a palindrome.\n            Accepts a JSON request with text, optional normalize, and save flags.\n            \\\"\\\"\\\"\n            try:\n                result = self.checker.is_palindrome(\n                    text=request.text,\n                    normalize=request.normalize,\n                    save=request.save\n                )\n                return result\n            except InvalidInputError as e:\n                logger.warning(f\"HTTP 400 Bad Request: {e}\")\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST, detail=str(e))\n            except RepositoryError as e:\n                logger.error(f\"HTTP 500 Repository Error: {e}\")\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=\"A server error occurred while processing the request (persistence failure).\")\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.critical(f\"An unhandled error occurred during check: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=\"An unexpected internal server error occurred.\")\n\n# Helper function to create the FastAPI app with dependency injection\ndef create_http_app() -> FastAPI:\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    Sets up dependencies and initializes the HTTPController's FastAPI app.\n    This function acts as the factory for the FastAPI application.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    config = Config() # Load config from environment or defaults\n    normalizer = Normalizer()\n    repository = SQLiteHistoryRepository(db_path=config.db_url.replace(\"sqlite:///\", \"\"))\n    checker = PalindromeChecker(normalizer=normalizer, repository=repository, config=config)\n    \n    controller = HTTPController(checker=checker)\n    return controller.app\n\"\"\"\n```"}
