{"task_id": "HumanEval/55", "solution": "def fib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return n-th Fibonacci number using the fast-doubling method.\n    This method efficiently computes F_n for large n values.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Define the fast-doubling helper function inline.\n    # This helper returns a tuple (F_k, F_{k+1})\n    def _fib_fast_doubling(k: int):\n        if k == 0:\n            return (0, 1)  # Base case: (F_0, F_1)\n\n        # Recursively compute (F_{k/2}, F_{k/2 + 1})\n        a, b = _fib_fast_doubling(k >> 1)  # k >> 1 is equivalent to k // 2\n\n        # Use the identities for F_{2m} and F_{2m+1}:\n        # F_{2m} = F_m * (2 * F_{m+1} - F_m)\n        # F_{2m+1} = F_m^2 + F_{m+1}^2\n        c = a * (2 * b - a)  # F_{2 * (k//2)}\n        d = a*a + b*b        # F_{2 * (k//2) + 1}\n\n        if k % 2 == 1:  # If k is odd, we need F_k = F_{2m+1}\n            return (d, c + d)  # Return (F_{2m+1}, F_{2m+2})\n        else:  # If k is even, we need F_k = F_{2m}\n            return (c, d)      # Return (F_{2m}, F_{2m+1})\n\n    # The result we need is F_n, which is the first element of the tuple for k=n.\n    return _fib_fast_doubling(n)[0]"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/56", "solution": "def correct_bracketing(brackets: str):\n    \"\"\" brackets is a string of \"<\" and \">\".\n    return True if every opening bracket has a corresponding closing bracket.\n    \"\"\"\n    balance = 0\n    for char in brackets:\n        if char == '<':\n            balance += 1\n        elif char == '>':\n            balance -= 1\n        # If balance drops below zero, a closing bracket appeared without a matching open one.\n        if balance < 0:\n            return False\n    # If balance is zero at the end, all brackets are matched.\n    return balance == 0"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/55", "solution": "```\n# File: src/fiblib/exceptions.py\nimport logging\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass FibonacciError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for Fibonacci library errors.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass InvalidInputError(FibonacciError):\n    \"\"\"Raised for invalid input parameters.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        logger.warning(f\"Invalid input error: {message}\")\n\nclass AlgorithmNotSupportedError(FibonacciError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an unsupported algorithm is requested.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, algorithm: str):\n        message = f\"Algorithm '{algorithm}' is not supported.\"\n        super().__init__(message)\n        logger.error(message)\n\nclass CacheError(FibonacciError):\n    \"\"\"Raised for errors interacting with the cache backend.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str, original_exception: Exception | None = None):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.original_exception = original_exception\n        logger.error(f\"Cache error: {message}, original: {original_exception}\")\n\n```\n# File: src/fiblib/config.py\nimport os\n\nclass Config:\n    \"\"\"Central configuration for the Fibonacci service.\"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_ALGORITHM: str = os.getenv(\"FIB_DEFAULT_ALGORITHM\", \"fast_doubling\")\n    CACHE_TTL_SECONDS: int = int(os.getenv(\"FIB_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS\", \"3600\"))\n    MAX_N: int = int(os.getenv(\"FIB_MAX_N\", \"10000000\"))\n    REDIS_URL: str | None = os.getenv(\"REDIS_URL\", None)\n    LOG_LEVEL: str = os.getenv(\"FIB_LOG_LEVEL\", \"INFO\")\n\ndef load_config() -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Loads configuration values into a dictionary.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"DEFAULT_ALGORITHM\": Config.DEFAULT_ALGORITHM,\n        \"CACHE_TTL_SECONDS\": Config.CACHE_TTL_SECONDS,\n        \"MAX_N\": Config.MAX_N,\n        \"REDIS_URL\": Config.REDIS_URL,\n        \"LOG_LEVEL\": Config.LOG_LEVEL,\n    }\n\n```\n# File: src/fiblib/utils.py\nimport logging\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\ndef validate_input(n: int, max_n: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Validates the input 'n' against non-negative and maximum allowed values.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise InvalidInputError(f\"Input 'n' must be an integer, got {type(n).__name__}.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(f\"Input 'n' must be non-negative, got {n}.\")\n    if n > max_n:\n        raise InvalidInputError(f\"Input 'n' exceeds maximum allowed value of {max_n}.\")\n    logger.debug(f\"Input n={n} validated successfully.\")\n\ndef key_for(n: int, algorithm: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Generates a cache key for a given n and algorithm.\"\"\"\n    return f\"fib:{algorithm}:{n}\"\n\n```\n# File: src/fiblib/algorithms.py\nimport abc\nfrom typing import Type, Dict\nfrom src.fiblib.exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass FibonacciAlgorithm(abc.ABC):\n    \"\"\"Abstract base class for Fibonacci number algorithms.\"\"\"\n    @abc.abstractmethod\n    def name(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Returns the canonical name of the algorithm.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    @abc.abstractmethod\n    def compute(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the n-th Fibonacci number.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\nclass IterativeAlgorithm(FibonacciAlgorithm):\n    \"\"\"Implements the Fibonacci sequence using an iterative approach.\"\"\"\n    def name(self) -> str:\n        return \"iterative\"\n\n    def compute(self, n: int) -> int:\n        if n < 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"n must be non-negative for iterative algorithm.\")\n        if n == 0:\n            return 0\n        a, b = 0, 1\n        for _ in range(n - 1):\n            a, b = b, a + b\n        return b\n\nclass FastDoublingAlgorithm(FibonacciAlgorithm):\n    \"\"\"Computes the Fibonacci sequence using the fast doubling method.\"\"\"\n    def name(self) -> str:\n        return \"fast_doubling\"\n\n    def compute(self, n: int) -> int:\n        if n < 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"n must be non-negative for fast-doubling algorithm.\")\n        return self._fast_doubling(n)[0]\n\n    def _fast_doubling(self, n: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Helper function for fast doubling, returns (F(n), F(n+1)).\"\"\"\n        if n == 0:\n            return (0, 1)\n        a, b = self._fast_doubling(n // 2)\n        # F(2k) = F(k) * (2*F(k+1) - F(k))\n        c = a * (2 * b - a)\n        # F(2k+1) = F(k)^2 + F(k+1)^2\n        d = a * a + b * b\n        if n % 2 == 0:\n            return (c, d)\n        else:\n            return (d, c + d)\n\nclass MatrixAlgorithm(FibonacciAlgorithm):\n    \"\"\"Computes the Fibonacci sequence using matrix exponentiation.\"\"\"\n    def name(self) -> str:\n        return \"matrix\"\n\n    def compute(self, n: int) -> int:\n        if n < 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"n must be non-negative for matrix algorithm.\")\n        if n == 0:\n            return 0\n        if n == 1:\n            return 1\n        \n        # Base matrix [[1, 1], [1, 0]]\n        F = [[1, 1], [1, 0]]\n        self._matrix_pow(F, n - 1)\n        return F[0][0]\n\n    def _matrix_multiply(self, A: list[list[int]], B: list[list[int]]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Helper to multiply two 2x2 matrices and store result in A.\"\"\"\n        x = A[0][0] * B[0][0] + A[0][1] * B[1][0]\n        y = A[0][0] * B[0][1] + A[0][1] * B[1][1]\n        z = A[1][0] * B[0][0] + A[1][1] * B[1][0]\n        w = A[1][0] * B[0][1] + A[1][1] * B[1][1]\n        A[0][0], A[0][1], A[1][0], A[1][1] = x, y, z, w\n\n    def _matrix_pow(self, F: list[list[int]], n: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Helper to compute F^n using binary exponentiation (for 2x2 matrix).\"\"\"\n        M = [[1, 1], [1, 0]]\n        if n == 0 or n == 1:\n            return\n        self._matrix_pow(F, n // 2)\n        self._matrix_multiply(F, F)\n        if n % 2 != 0:\n            self._matrix_multiply(F, M)\n\nALGORITHM_REGISTRY: Dict[str, Type[FibonacciAlgorithm]] = {\n    \"iterative\": IterativeAlgorithm,\n    \"fast_doubling\": FastDoublingAlgorithm,\n    \"matrix\": MatrixAlgorithm,\n}\n\n```\n# File: src/fiblib/factory.py\nfrom typing import Type\nfrom src.fiblib.algorithms import FibonacciAlgorithm, ALGORITHM_REGISTRY\nfrom src.fiblib.exceptions import AlgorithmNotSupportedError\nfrom src.fiblib.config import load_config\n\nclass AlgorithmFactory:\n    \"\"\"Factory for creating FibonacciAlgorithm instances.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._config = load_config()\n\n    def get_algorithm(self, name: str | None) -> FibonacciAlgorithm:\n        \"\"\"Returns an algorithm instance by name, or the default if name is None.\"\"\"\n        algo_name = name if name is not None else self._config[\"DEFAULT_ALGORITHM\"]\n        algo_cls = ALGORITHM_REGISTRY.get(algo_name)\n        if algo_cls is None:\n            raise AlgorithmNotSupportedError(algo_name)\n        return algo_cls()\n\n```\n# File: src/fiblib/cache.py\nimport abc\nimport time\nimport threading\nimport logging\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom src.fiblib.exceptions import CacheError\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass CacheAdapter(abc.ABC):\n    \"\"\"Abstract base class for cache adapters.\"\"\"\n    @abc.abstractmethod\n    def get(self, key: str) -> Optional[str]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a value from the cache by key.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    @abc.abstractmethod\n    def set(self, key: str, value: str, ttl: int | None) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stores a value in the cache with an optional time-to-live.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\nclass InMemoryCache(CacheAdapter):\n    \"\"\"An in-memory cache with TTL support, suitable for testing or single-process use.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._store: dict[str, tuple[str, float]] = {}  # value, expiry_ts\n        self._lock = threading.Lock()\n\n    def get(self, key: str) -> Optional[str]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a value if not expired.\"\"\"\n        with self._lock:\n            entry = self._store.get(key)\n            if entry is None:\n                logger.debug(f\"Cache MISS for key: {key}\")\n                return None\n            value, expiry_ts = entry\n            if expiry_ts == 0 or expiry_ts > time.monotonic():  # 0 means no expiry\n                logger.debug(f\"Cache HIT for key: {key}\")\n                return value\n            else:\n                del self._store[key]  # Expired\n                logger.debug(f\"Cache EXPIRED for key: {key}\")\n                return None\n\n    def set(self, key: str, value: str, ttl: int | None) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stores a value with given TTL.\"\"\"\n        with self._lock:\n            expiry_ts = time.monotonic() + ttl if ttl is not None else 0\n            self._store[key] = (value, expiry_ts)\n            logger.debug(f\"Cache SET key: {key}, ttl: {ttl}\")\n\nclass RedisCache(CacheAdapter):\n    \"\"\"A Redis-backed cache adapter using the redis-py library.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, redis_url: str):\n        try:\n            import redis\n            self._client = redis.from_url(redis_url, decode_responses=True)\n            self._client.ping() # Test connection\n            logger.info(\"Successfully connected to Redis.\")\n        except ImportError:\n            raise CacheError(\"redis-py not installed. Please install with `pip install redis`.\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise CacheError(f\"Failed to connect to Redis at {redis_url}.\", original_exception=e)\n\n    def get(self, key: str) -> Optional[str]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a value from Redis.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            value = self._client.get(key)\n            if value is not None:\n                logger.debug(f\"Redis HIT for key: {key}\")\n            else:\n                logger.debug(f\"Redis MISS for key: {key}\")\n            return value\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise CacheError(f\"Error getting key '{key}' from Redis.\", original_exception=e)\n\n    def set(self, key: str, value: str, ttl: int | None) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stores a value in Redis with optional TTL.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            if ttl is not None:\n                self._client.setex(key, ttl, value)\n            else:\n                self._client.set(key, value)\n            logger.debug(f\"Redis SET key: {key}, ttl: {ttl}\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise CacheError(f\"Error setting key '{key}' in Redis.\", original_exception=e)\n\n```\n# File: src/fiblib/repository.py\nimport abc\nfrom typing import Optional, Tuple, Dict\nimport logging\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass MemoRepository(abc.ABC):\n    \"\"\"Abstract interface for a persistent memoization repository.\"\"\"\n    @abc.abstractmethod\n    def get(self, n: int, algorithm: str) -> Optional[int]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a previously computed Fibonacci value.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    @abc.abstractmethod\n    def set(self, n: int, algorithm: str, value: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stores a computed Fibonacci value.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\nclass InMemoryRepo(MemoRepository):\n    \"\"\"An in-memory repository for memoization, primarily for testing.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._data: Dict[Tuple[int, str], int] = {}\n\n    def get(self, n: int, algorithm: str) -> Optional[int]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a value from the in-memory store.\"\"\"\n        key = (n, algorithm)\n        value = self._data.get(key)\n        if value is not None:\n            logger.debug(f\"Repo HIT for {key}\")\n        else:\n            logger.debug(f\"Repo MISS for {key}\")\n        return value\n\n    def set(self, n: int, algorithm: str, value: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stores a value in the in-memory store.\"\"\"\n        key = (n, algorithm)\n        self._data[key] = value\n        logger.debug(f\"Repo SET {key} = {value}\")\n\n# RedisRepo would be similar to RedisCache, but store (n, algo) -> int\n# For simplicity and given the focus on Cache, this is omitted unless explicitly requested.\n\n```\n# File: src/fiblib/service.py\nimport logging\nfrom src.fiblib.cache import CacheAdapter, CacheError\nfrom src.fiblib.factory import AlgorithmFactory\nfrom src.fiblib.repository import MemoRepository\nfrom src.fiblib.utils import validate_input, key_for\nfrom src.fiblib.exceptions import FibonacciError\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass FibonacciService:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates Fibonacci computation, handling validation, caching, and algorithm selection.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, cache: CacheAdapter | None, factory: AlgorithmFactory, repo: MemoRepository | None, config: dict):\n        self._cache = cache\n        self._factory = factory\n        self._repo = repo\n        self._config = config\n        logger.info(\"FibonacciService initialized.\")\n\n    def compute(self, n: int, algorithm: str | None = None) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the n-th Fibonacci number, utilizing cache and repository.\"\"\"\n        validate_input(n, self._config[\"MAX_N\"])\n        algo_name = algorithm or self._config[\"DEFAULT_ALGORITHM\"]\n        cache_key = key_for(n, algo_name)\n\n        # 1. Try cache\n        if self._cache:\n            try:\n                cached = self._cache.get(cache_key)\n                if cached is not None:\n                    logger.debug(f\"Returning cached value for n={n}, algo={algo_name}\")\n                    return int(cached)\n            except CacheError:\n                logger.warning(f\"Cache error during GET for key {cache_key}, proceeding with computation.\")\n        \n        # 2. Try repository (if present)\n        if self._repo:\n            stored = self._repo.get(n, algo_name)\n            if stored is not None:\n                logger.debug(f\"Returning repository value for n={n}, algo={algo_name}\")\n                # Optionally update cache if repo hit but cache miss\n                if self._cache:\n                    try:\n                        self._cache.set(cache_key, str(stored), self._config[\"CACHE_TTL_SECONDS\"])\n                    except CacheError:\n                        logger.warning(f\"Cache error during SET for key {cache_key} after repo hit.\")\n                return stored\n\n        # 3. Compute\n        algo_instance = self._factory.get_algorithm(algo_name)\n        value = algo_instance.compute(n)\n        logger.debug(f\"Computed value {value} for n={n}, algo={algo_name}\")\n\n        # 4. Store in cache\n        if self._cache:\n            try:\n                self._cache.set(cache_key, str(value), self._config[\"CACHE_TTL_SECONDS\"])\n            except CacheError:\n                logger.warning(f\"Cache error during SET for key {cache_key} after computation.\")\n\n        # 5. Store in repository\n        if self._repo:\n            try:\n                self._repo.set(n, algo_name, value)\n            except Exception as e: # Catch all for repo persistence issues\n                logger.error(f\"Repository error during SET for n={n}, algo={algo_name}: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n\n        return value\n\n```\n# File: src/fiblib/models.py\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict\n\nclass FibonacciRequest:\n    \"\"\"Data Transfer Object for Fibonacci number requests.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, n: int, algorithm: Optional[str] = None):\n        self.n = n\n        self.algorithm = algorithm\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, data: Dict) -> \"FibonacciRequest\":\n        \"\"\"Creates a FibonacciRequest instance from a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        n = data.get(\"n\")\n        if not isinstance(n, int):\n            raise ValueError(\"Field 'n' must be an integer.\")\n        return cls(n=n, algorithm=data.get(\"algorithm\"))\n\nclass FibonacciResponse:\n    \"\"\"Data Transfer Object for Fibonacci number responses.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, n: int, value: int, algorithm: str):\n        self.n = n\n        self.value = value\n        self.algorithm = algorithm\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> Dict:\n        \"\"\"Converts the response object to a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return {\"n\": self.n, \"value\": self.value, \"algorithm\": self.algorithm}\n\n```\n# File: src/fiblib/logging_config.py\nimport logging\nimport sys\n\ndef configure_logging(level: str = \"INFO\") -> None:\n    \"\"\"Configures basic logging for the application.\"\"\"\n    log_level = getattr(logging, level.upper(), logging.INFO)\n    logging.basicConfig(\n        level=log_level,\n        format='%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s',\n        stream=sys.stdout\n    )\n    # Set log level for uvicorn access logs\n    logging.getLogger(\"uvicorn.access\").setLevel(logging.WARNING)\n    logging.getLogger(\"uvicorn.error\").setLevel(log_level)\n    logging.getLogger(\"fastapi\").setLevel(log_level)\n    logging.info(f\"Logging configured at {level} level.\")\n\n```\n# File: src/fiblib/controller.py\nimport sys\nimport argparse\nimport logging\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, Request\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\n\nfrom src.fiblib.service import FibonacciService\nfrom src.fiblib.models import FibonacciRequest, FibonacciResponse\nfrom src.fiblib.exceptions import InvalidInputError, AlgorithmNotSupportedError, FibonacciError\nfrom src.fiblib.config import load_config\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Controller for handling command-line interface requests.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: FibonacciService):\n        self._service = service\n        self._config = load_config()\n\n    def run(self, argv: list[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Parses CLI arguments and executes the requested command.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"fibcli\",\n            description=\"Compute Fibonacci numbers via CLI.\"\n        )\n        subparsers = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", required=True)\n\n        compute_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\"compute\", help=\"Compute the N-th Fibonacci number.\")\n        compute_parser.add_argument(\"n\", type=int, help=\"The non-negative integer N.\")\n        compute_parser.add_argument(\n            \"--algorithm\",\n            type=str,\n            default=self._config[\"DEFAULT_ALGORITHM\"],\n            help=f\"Algorithm to use (default: {self._config['DEFAULT_ALGORITHM']}).\"\n        )\n\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv[1:])\n\n        if args.command == \"compute\":\n            return self._handle_compute(args.n, args.algorithm)\n        return 1 # Should not reach here if command is required\n\n    def _handle_compute(self, n: int, algorithm: str | None) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Handles the 'compute' CLI command.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            result = self._service.compute(n, algorithm)\n            print(result)\n            return 0\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            logger.error(f\"CLI Error: {e}\")\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2 # Invalid input exit code\n        except AlgorithmNotSupportedError as e:\n            logger.error(f\"CLI Error: {e}\")\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        except FibonacciError as e:\n            logger.error(f\"CLI Internal Error: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n            print(f\"An internal error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # General error exit code\n\nAPI_PREFIX = \"/api/v1\"\n\nclass HTTPController:\n    \"\"\"Controller for handling HTTP API requests using FastAPI.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: FibonacciService):\n        self._service = service\n        self.app = self._create_app()\n        logger.info(\"HTTPController initialized.\")\n\n    def _create_app(self) -> FastAPI:\n        \"\"\"Creates and configures the FastAPI application.\"\"\"\n        app = FastAPI(\n            title=\"Fibonacci API\",\n            description=\"A simple API for computing Fibonacci numbers.\",\n            version=\"1.0.0\"\n        )\n\n        @app.post(f\"{API_PREFIX}/fibonacci\")\n        async def compute_fib(request_data: dict):\n            \"\"\"Endpoint to compute the N-th Fibonacci number.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                fr = FibonacciRequest.from_dict(request_data)\n                value = self._service.compute(fr.n, fr.algorithm)\n                # Use the actual algorithm used for the response\n                actual_algo = fr.algorithm or self._service._config[\"DEFAULT_ALGORITHM\"]\n                resp = FibonacciResponse(n=fr.n, value=value, algorithm=actual_algo)\n                logger.info(f\"HTTP request for n={fr.n}, algo={fr.algorithm} successful.\")\n                return JSONResponse(content=resp.to_dict(), status_code=200)\n            except (ValueError, InvalidInputError, AlgorithmNotSupportedError) as e:\n                logger.warning(f\"HTTP 400 Bad Request: {e}\")\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=str(e))\n            except FibonacciError as e:\n                logger.exception(f\"HTTP 500 Internal Server Error: {e}\")\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"An internal server error occurred.\")\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.exception(f\"Unhandled HTTP error: {e}\")\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"An unexpected error occurred.\")\n        \n        @app.get(\"/health\")\n        async def health_check():\n            \"\"\"Health check endpoint.\"\"\"\n            return {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n\n        return app\n\n```\n# File: src/fiblib/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\nFibonacci Library: A reliable, testable Python library and service for computing Fibonacci numbers.\nSupports multiple algorithms, caching, and exposes functionality via library API, CLI, and HTTP.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom src.fiblib.service import FibonacciService\nfrom src.fiblib.algorithms import IterativeAlgorithm, FastDoublingAlgorithm, MatrixAlgorithm, FibonacciAlgorithm\nfrom src.fiblib.cache import InMemoryCache, RedisCache, CacheAdapter\nfrom src.fiblib.repository import InMemoryRepo, MemoRepository\nfrom src.fiblib.factory import AlgorithmFactory\nfrom src.fiblib.config import load_config\nfrom src.fiblib.exceptions import FibonacciError, InvalidInputError, AlgorithmNotSupportedError, CacheError\nfrom src.fiblib.controller import CLIController, HTTPController\nfrom src.fiblib.logging_config import configure_logging\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n\n# Configure logging immediately on package import for standalone scripts or CLI\nconfigure_logging(load_config()[\"LOG_LEVEL\"])\n\n# Initialize default factory and config\n_config = load_config()\n_algorithm_factory = AlgorithmFactory()\n_cache_adapter: CacheAdapter | None = None\n_repo_adapter: MemoRepository | None = None\n\nif _config[\"REDIS_URL\"]:\n    try:\n        _cache_adapter = RedisCache(_config[\"REDIS_URL\"])\n        # If Redis is used for cache, might also use it for repo if desired,\n        # but sticking to InMemoryRepo as default unless specified.\n    except CacheError as e:\n        # Log the error but allow the service to run without Redis cache\n        logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n        logger.warning(f\"Could not connect to Redis: {e}. Falling back to in-memory cache if needed.\")\n        _cache_adapter = InMemoryCache() # Fallback for Redis issues, but only if an error occurred\n\n# If no Redis, or Redis connection failed, use InMemoryCache as default\nif _cache_adapter is None:\n    _cache_adapter = InMemoryCache()\n_repo_adapter = InMemoryRepo() # Default to in-memory for repo\n\nfibonacci_service = FibonacciService(\n    cache=_cache_adapter,\n    factory=_algorithm_factory,\n    repo=_repo_adapter,\n    config=_config\n)\n\ndef compute(n: int, algorithm: str | None = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Public API for computing the n-th Fibonacci number.\n    Uses the configured FibonacciService instance.\n    \"\"\"\n    return fibonacci_service.compute(n, algorithm)\n\ndef create_cli_controller() -> CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Creates a CLIController instance with the default FibonacciService.\"\"\"\n    return CLIController(fibonacci_service)\n\ndef create_http_controller() -> HTTPController:\n    \"\"\"Creates an HTTPController instance with the default FibonacciService.\"\"\"\n    return HTTPController(fibonacci_service)\n\n# Expose key components directly for library users\n__all__ = [\n    \"compute\",\n    \"FibonacciService\",\n    \"FibonacciAlgorithm\",\n    \"IterativeAlgorithm\",\n    \"FastDoublingAlgorithm\",\n    \"MatrixAlgorithm\",\n    \"AlgorithmFactory\",\n    \"CacheAdapter\",\n    \"InMemoryCache\",\n    \"RedisCache\",\n    \"MemoRepository\",\n    \"InMemoryRepo\",\n    \"FibonacciError\",\n    \"InvalidInputError\",\n    \"AlgorithmNotSupportedError\",\n    \"CacheError\",\n    \"CLIController\",\n    \"HTTPController\",\n    \"load_config\",\n    \"configure_logging\",\n    \"fibonacci_service\" # Expose the default service instance\n]\n\n```\n# File: pyproject.toml\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"fiblib\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A reliable Python library and service for computing Fibonacci numbers.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"fiblib\", from = \"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \"^3.10\"\nfastapi = \"^0.111.0\"\nuvicorn = {extras = [\"standard\"], version = \"^0.29.0\"}\nredis = {version = \"^5.0.0\", optional = true}\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^8.2.0\"\nruff = \"^0.4.4\"\n\n[tool.poetry.extras]\nredis = [\"redis\"]\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\nfibcli = \"fiblib.__main__:main_cli\"\n\n[tool.poetry.urls]\nHomepage = \"https://github.com/yourusername/fiblib\"\nRepository = \"https://github.com/yourusername/fiblib\"\n\"Bug Tracker\" = \"https://github.com/yourusername/fiblib/issues\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n```\n# File: src/fiblib/__main__.py\n\"\"\"\nEntry points for the fiblib package.\nThis module handles both CLI and HTTP service startup.\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\nimport uvicorn\nfrom src.fiblib import create_cli_controller, create_http_controller, configure_logging, load_config\n\ndef main_cli():\n    \"\"\"Main entry point for the CLI application.\"\"\"\n    config = load_config()\n    configure_logging(config[\"LOG_LEVEL\"])\n    cli_controller = create_cli_controller()\n    sys.exit(cli_controller.run(sys.argv))\n\ndef main_http():\n    \"\"\"Main entry point for the HTTP service application.\"\"\"\n    config = load_config()\n    configure_logging(config[\"LOG_LEVEL\"])\n    http_controller = create_http_controller()\n    uvicorn.run(http_controller.app, host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=8000)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # This block is mainly for direct execution during development\n    # In production, `poetry run fibcli` or `uvicorn fiblib.__main__:http_controller.app` would be used.\n    # We can default to HTTP service if no args, or a placeholder for now\n    print(\"Run `poetry run fibcli compute <n>` for CLI or `poetry run fibhttp` for HTTP service.\")\n\n# Alias for uvicorn to pick up the app\nhttp_app = create_http_controller().app\n\n```\n# File: README.md\n# Fibonacci Library and Service (fiblib)\n\n`fiblib` is a Python library and service for computing the n-th Fibonacci number. It supports multiple algorithms, caching, and provides a programmatic API, a command-line interface (CLI), and a simple HTTP JSON endpoint.\n\n## Features\n\n-   **Multiple Algorithms**: Iterative, Fast Doubling, and Matrix exponentiation.\n-   **Caching**: In-memory and Redis cache adapters to optimize repeated calls.\n-   **Flexible Access**:\n    -   Python Library API: `fiblib.compute(n)`\n    -   CLI: `fibcli compute <n>`\n    -   HTTP JSON API: `POST /api/v1/fibonacci`\n-   **Configurable**: Switch algorithms, cache backend, and other parameters via config or environment variables.\n-   **Robust**: Input validation and error handling.\n-   **Testable**: Modular design with dependency injection.\n\n## Installation\n\n### Requirements\n\n-   Python 3.10+\n-   Poetry (recommended for development)\n\n### Setup with Poetry\n\n1.  **Clone the repository:**\n    ```bash\n    git clone https://github.com/yourusername/fiblib.git\n    cd fiblib\n    ```\n2.  **Install dependencies:**\n    ```bash\n    poetry install\n    ```\n3.  **For Redis cache (optional):**\n    ```bash\n    poetry install -E redis\n    ```\n\n## Usage\n\n### 1. Library API\n\nYou can import `fiblib` and use it directly in your Python code:\n\n```python\nimport fiblib\n\n# Compute with default algorithm (fast_doubling)\nn_10 = fiblib.compute(10)\nprint(f\"Fib(10) = {n_10}\") # Output: Fib(10) = 55\n\n# Specify an algorithm\nn_20_iterative = fiblib.compute(20, algorithm=\"iterative\")\nprint(f\"Fib(20) (iterative) = {n_20_iterative}\") # Output: Fib(20) (iterative) = 6765\n\n# Access the underlying service or factory for advanced use\nfrom fiblib import fibonacci_service, AlgorithmFactory, InMemoryCache\n\n# Example of custom service initialization (for testing/advanced usage)\nmy_config = fiblib.load_config()\nmy_factory = AlgorithmFactory()\nmy_cache = InMemoryCache()\nmy_service = fiblib.FibonacciService(cache=my_cache, factory=my_factory, repo=None, config=my_config)\nvalue = my_service.compute(5)\nprint(f\"Fib(5) via custom service = {value}\") # Output: Fib(5) via custom service = 5\n```\n\n### 2. Command-Line Interface (CLI)\n\nUse the `fibcli` command installed by Poetry:\n\n```bash\n# Compute with default algorithm (fast_doubling)\npoetry run fibcli compute 10\n# Output: 55\n\n# Specify an algorithm\npoetry run fibcli compute 100 --algorithm iterative\n# Output: 354224848179261915075\n\n# Invalid input\npoetry run fibcli compute -5\n# Output: Error: Input 'n' must be non-negative, got -5.\n```\n\n### 3. HTTP JSON API\n\nThe HTTP service is built with FastAPI and served by Uvicorn.\n\n1.  **Start the service:**\n    ```bash\n    poetry run uvicorn src.fiblib.__main__:http_app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --reload\n    ```\n    (Remove `--reload` for production environments).\n\n2.  **Make a POST request:**\n    Use `curl` or any HTTP client to send a POST request to `/api/v1/fibonacci`.\n\n    ```bash\n    # Example using curl with default algorithm\n    curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/fibonacci \\\n         -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n         -d '{\"n\": 10}'\n\n    # Expected response (JSON):\n    # {\"n\":10,\"value\":55,\"algorithm\":\"fast_doubling\"}\n\n    # Example using curl with a specified algorithm\n    curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/fibonacci \\\n         -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n         -d '{\"n\": 50, \"algorithm\": \"iterative\"}'\n\n    # Expected response (JSON):\n    # {\"n\":50,\"value\":12586269025,\"algorithm\":\"iterative\"}\n\n    # Example for invalid input\n    curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/fibonacci \\\n         -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n         -d '{\"n\": -1}'\n\n    # Expected response (JSON, status 400):\n    # {\"detail\":\"Input 'n' must be non-negative, got -1.\"}\n    ```\n3. **Health Check**:\n    ```bash\n    curl http://localhost:8000/health\n    # Expected response (JSON):\n    # {\"status\":\"ok\"}\n    ```\n\n## Configuration\n\nThe application can be configured using environment variables:\n\n-   `FIB_DEFAULT_ALGORITHM`: Sets the default algorithm (e.g., `iterative`, `fast_doubling`, `matrix`). Default: `fast_doubling`.\n-   `FIB_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS`: Sets the cache time-to-live in seconds. Default: `3600`.\n-   `FIB_MAX_N`: Sets the maximum allowed value for `n`. Default: `10000000`.\n-   `REDIS_URL`: If set (e.g., `redis://localhost:6379/0`), enables Redis caching. Otherwise, an in-memory cache is used.\n-   `FIB_LOG_LEVEL`: Sets the logging level (e.g., `DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING`, `ERROR`). Default: `INFO`.\n\nExample:\n\n```bash\nREDIS_URL=\"redis://localhost:6379/0\" FIB_DEFAULT_ALGORITHM=\"iterative\" poetry run fibcli compute 10\n```\n\n## Development\n\n### Running Tests\n\nUnit and integration tests are located in the `tests/` directory.\n\n```bash\npoetry run pytest\n```\n\n### Linting\n\nWe use `ruff` for linting and code formatting.\n\n```bash\npoetry run ruff check src/ tests/\npoetry run ruff format src/ tests/\n```\n\n### Building the Package\n\n```bash\npoetry build\n```\nThis will create `dist/*.whl` and `dist/*.tar.gz` files.\n\n---"}
