{"task_id": "HumanEval/71", "solution": "```python\nfrom math import sqrt\n\ndef triangle_area(a, b, c):\n    '''\n    Computes the area of a triangle given its three side lengths.\n    Returns the area rounded to two decimal places, or -1 if the sides are invalid.\n    '''\n    # Check for positive side lengths and triangle inequality\n    if not (a > 0 and b > 0 and c > 0 and\n            a + b > c and a + c > b and b + c > a):\n        return -1.0\n\n    # Calculate the semi-perimeter\n    s = (a + b + c) / 2.0\n\n    # Calculate the value under the square root in Heron's formula\n    val_under_sqrt = s * (s - a) * (s - b) * (s - c)\n\n    # If the value under the square root is negative (due to floating point inaccuracies for\n    # nearly degenerate triangles), the triangle is considered invalid.\n    if val_under_sqrt < 0:\n        return -1.0\n\n    # Calculate the area and round to two decimal places\n    area = sqrt(val_under_sqrt)\n    return round(area, 2)\n```"}
