{"task_id": "HumanEval/71", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef triangle_area(a, b, c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the area of a triangle given three side lengths, rounded to 2 decimals.\n    Returns -1 if the sides do not form a valid triangle or if computation fails.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate side lengths for positivity and triangle inequality.\n    if not (a > 0 and b > 0 and c > 0 and\n            a + b > c and a + c > b and b + c > a):\n        return -1\n\n    # Calculate the semi-perimeter.\n    s = (a + b + c) / 2.0\n\n    # Apply Heron's formula to find the area squared.\n    # Clamp area_sq to 0 to handle minor floating point inaccuracies that might yield negative values.\n    area_sq = s * (s - a) * (s - b) * (s - c)\n    area = math.sqrt(max(area_sq, 0.0))\n\n    # Round the area to two decimal places, adding a small epsilon to mitigate rounding errors.\n    rounded_area = round(area + 1e-12, 2)\n\n    # Return -1 if the computed area is not a finite number (e.g., NaN or infinity).\n    if math.isinf(rounded_area) or math.isnan(rounded_area):\n        return -1\n    return rounded_area\n```"}
