{"task_id": "HumanEval/90", "solution": "def next_smallest(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the 2nd smallest distinct element from a list, or None if not available.\n    Assumes input is a list of integers as per specification.\n    \"\"\"\n    min1 = float('inf') # Smallest distinct element found so far\n    min2 = float('inf') # Second smallest distinct element found so far\n\n    for v in lst:\n        if v < min1:\n            # Found a new smallest distinct element\n            min2 = min1\n            min1 = v\n        elif v != min1 and v < min2:\n            # Found a new second smallest distinct element (v is distinct from min1)\n            min2 = v\n\n    if min2 == float('inf'):\n        return None\n    else:\n        return min2"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/91", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef is_bored(S):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts \"boredoms\" where a boredom is a sentence starting with \"I\".\n    Sentences are delimited by '.', '?' or '!'.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    boredom_count = 0\n    \n    # Normalize the entire input string first.\n    # This replaces multiple whitespace characters with a single space\n    # and removes any leading or trailing whitespace from the whole string.\n    normalized_S = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', S).strip()\n\n    # Split the normalized text into potential sentence fragments.\n    # Sentences are delimited by '.', '?', or '!' characters.\n    fragments = re.split(r'[.?!]', normalized_S)\n\n    for fragment in fragments:\n        # Trim leading/trailing whitespace from each fragment to get a clean sentence.\n        # This also effectively handles empty fragments that result from multiple delimiters\n        # or delimiters at the very start or end of the input string.\n        sentence_text = fragment.strip()\n\n        # Proceed only if the trimmed sentence is not an empty string.\n        if sentence_text:\n            # Tokenize the sentence by whitespace to find the first word.\n            # We explicitly check if the split list is not empty to prevent IndexError.\n            first_token_list = sentence_text.split()\n            first_token = first_token_list[0] if first_token_list else \"\"\n\n            # Increment the boredom count if the first token is exactly \"I\" (case-sensitive).\n            if first_token == \"I\":\n                boredom_count += 1\n\n    return boredom_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/91", "solution": "import re\n\ndef is_bored(S):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts sentences starting with \"I\", delimited by '.', '?' or '!'.\n    Robust to whitespace and leading punctuation/quotes of the first word.\n    \"\"\"\n    boredom_count = 0\n    \n    # Define characters considered \"leading punctuation/quotes\" to be trimmed from sentence start.\n    PUNCTUATION_TO_STRIP_FROM_SENTENCE_START = \"'\\\"([{ \"\n\n    # Normalize whitespace: replace multiple whitespace chars with a single space and trim.\n    normalized_s = ' '.join(S.split())\n\n    # Split text into sentences using '.', '?' or '!' as delimiters.\n    # This will produce empty strings for consecutive delimiters or leading/trailing ones,\n    # which will be handled by subsequent trimming and checks.\n    raw_sentences = re.split(r'[.!?]', normalized_s)\n\n    for sentence_text in raw_sentences:\n        # Trim leading/trailing whitespace from the potential sentence.\n        trimmed_sentence = sentence_text.strip()\n        \n        # Skip if the sentence is empty after trimming.\n        if not trimmed_sentence:\n            continue\n\n        # Strip leading punctuation/quotes from the start of the sentence.\n        # This handles cases like '\"I am here\"' becoming 'I am here'.\n        cleaned_sentence_start = trimmed_sentence.lstrip(PUNCTUATION_TO_STRIP_FROM_SENTENCE_START)\n\n        # Split the cleaned sentence part into words, taking only the first one if it exists.\n        words = cleaned_sentence_start.split(maxsplit=1)\n\n        if words:\n            first_token = words[0]\n            # Check if the first token is exactly \"I\" (case-sensitive).\n            # This correctly differentiates \"I\" from \"i\" or \"I'm\".\n            if first_token == \"I\":\n                boredom_count += 1\n                \n    return boredom_count"}
