{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "def x_or_y(n, x, y):\n    \"\"\"A simple program which should return the value of x if n is \n    a prime number and should return the value of y otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def is_prime(num):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a non-negative integer is prime using trial division.\"\"\"\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        if num == 2 or num == 3:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0 or num % 3 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 5\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0 or num % (i + 2) == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 6\n        return True\n\n    if is_prime(n):\n        return x\n    else:\n        return y"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "def x_or_y(n, x, y):\n    \"\"\"Returns x if n is prime, otherwise y.\n    This includes an inline primality test for integer n.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def is_prime_local(num):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a non-negative integer is prime.\"\"\"\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        if num == 2 or num == 3:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0 or num % 3 == 0:\n            return False\n        \n        # Optimized trial division using 6k +/- 1 rule\n        i = 5\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0 or num % (i + 2) == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 6\n        return True\n\n    if is_prime_local(n):\n        return x\n    else:\n        return y"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/151", "solution": "```python\ndef double_the_difference(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of squares of odd, non-negative integers in a list.\n    Ignores negative numbers and non-integer values.\n    \"\"\"\n    total = 0\n    for x in lst:\n        # Check if the number is non-negative, has no fractional part, and is odd.\n        if x >= 0 and x % 1 == 0 and int(x) % 2 != 0:\n            total += int(x) * int(x)\n    return total\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/151", "solution": "```python\ndef double_the_difference(lst):\n    '''\n    Given a list of numbers, return the sum of squares of the numbers in the list that are odd.\n    Negative numbers are ignored.\n    \n    double_the_difference([1, 3, 2, 0]) == 10\n    double_the_difference([-1, -2, 0]) == 0\n    double_the_difference([9, -2]) == 81\n    double_the_difference([0]) == 0  \n   \n    If the input list is empty, return 0.\n    '''\n    total_sum = 0\n    for num in lst:\n        # Only consider non-negative numbers.\n        if num >= 0:\n            # Add square if the number is odd.\n            if num % 2 != 0:\n                total_sum += num * num\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/152", "solution": "def compare(game,guess):\n    \"\"\"\n    Compares two arrays of scores and guesses to determine deviation per match.\n    Returns an array where 0 means an exact match and a positive integer is the absolute difference.\n    \"\"\"\n    diffs = []\n    for i in range(len(game)):\n        if game[i] == guess[i]:\n            diffs.append(0)\n        else:\n            diffs.append(abs(game[i] - guess[i]))\n    return diffs"}
