{"task_id": "HumanEval/160", "solution": "def do_algebra(operator, operand):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given two lists operator, and operand, build and evaluate an algebraic expression.\n    This function processes the expression respecting operator precedence and associativity.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Define operator precedence and associativity rules for the shunting-yard algorithm\n    PRECEDENCE = {\"**\": 4, \"*\": 3, \"//\": 3, \"+\": 2, \"-\": 2}\n    RIGHT_ASSOCIATIVE = {\"**\"}\n\n    # Interleave operands and operators into a single token list for processing\n    # Example: [operand1, operator1, operand2, operator2, operand3]\n    tokens = []\n    for i in range(len(operator)):\n        tokens.append(operand[i])\n        tokens.append(operator[i])\n    tokens.append(operand[-1])\n\n    # Shunting-Yard algorithm to convert infix tokens to Postfix (Reverse Polish Notation)\n    output_queue = []\n    operator_stack = []\n\n    for token in tokens:\n        if isinstance(token, int):  # If the token is an integer (operand)\n            output_queue.append(token)\n        else:  # If the token is a string (operator)\n            # Pop operators from stack to output queue based on precedence and associativity\n            while (operator_stack and operator_stack[-1] in PRECEDENCE and\n                   ((token not in RIGHT_ASSOCIATIVE and PRECEDENCE[token] <= PRECEDENCE[operator_stack[-1]]) or\n                    (token in RIGHT_ASSOCIATIVE and PRECEDENCE[token] < PRECEDENCE[operator_stack[-1]]))):\n                output_queue.append(operator_stack.pop())\n            operator_stack.append(token)\n\n    # Pop any remaining operators from the stack to the output queue\n    while operator_stack:\n        output_queue.append(operator_stack.pop())\n\n    # Evaluate the Postfix (RPN) expression using a stack\n    evaluation_stack = []\n    for token in output_queue:\n        if isinstance(token, int):  # If the token is an integer (operand)\n            evaluation_stack.append(token)\n        else:  # If the token is a string (operator)\n            # For binary operations, pop operands in correct order (right then left)\n            b = evaluation_stack.pop()\n            a = evaluation_stack.pop()\n            \n            if token == '+':\n                result = a + b\n            elif token == '-':\n                result = a - b\n            elif token == '*':\n                result = a * b\n            elif token == '//':\n                result = a // b\n            elif token == '**':\n                result = a ** b\n            # Push the result of the operation back onto the stack\n            evaluation_stack.append(result)\n            \n    # The final result is the only item left on the evaluation stack\n    return evaluation_stack[0]"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/161", "solution": "def solve(s):\n    \"\"\"Reverses case of letters or reverses string if no letters.\n    The input `s` is assumed to be a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    has_letters = False\n    for char in s:\n        if char.isalpha():\n            has_letters = True\n            break\n\n    if has_letters:\n        result_chars = []\n        for char in s:\n            if char.islower():\n                result_chars.append(char.upper())\n            elif char.isupper():\n                result_chars.append(char.lower())\n            else:\n                result_chars.append(char)\n        return \"\".join(result_chars)\n    else:\n        return s[::-1}"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/160", "solution": "```python\ndef do_algebra(operator, operand):\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluates an algebraic expression constructed from lists of operators and operands,\n    respecting standard precedence and associativity.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Define operator properties: precedence and associativity.\n    _OP_PROPS = {\n        '**': {'precedence': 4, 'associativity': 'right'},\n        '*': {'precedence': 3, 'associativity': 'left'},\n        '//': {'precedence': 3, 'associativity': 'left'},\n        '+': {'precedence': 2, 'associativity': 'left'},\n        '-': {'precedence': 2, 'associativity': 'left'},\n    }\n\n    # Helper function to apply an operator to two operands.\n    def _apply_op(op_symbol, val1, val2):\n        if op_symbol == '+':\n            return val1 + val2\n        elif op_symbol == '-':\n            return val1 - val2\n        elif op_symbol == '*':\n            return val1 * val2\n        elif op_symbol == '//':\n            return val1 // val2\n        elif op_symbol == '**':\n            return pow(val1, val2)\n        # Trusting caller inputs, will not reach here for valid operators.\n\n    # Combine operands and operators into an infix token stream.\n    infix_tokens = []\n    for i in range(len(operand)):\n        infix_tokens.append(operand[i])\n        if i < len(operator):\n            infix_tokens.append(operator[i])\n\n    # Shunting-Yard Algorithm to convert infix to Reverse Polish Notation (RPN).\n    output_queue = []\n    operator_stack = []\n\n    for token in infix_tokens:\n        if isinstance(token, int):  # If it's an operand, add it to the output queue.\n            output_queue.append(token)\n        else:  # It's an operator\n            op1_symbol = token\n            op1_props = _OP_PROPS[op1_symbol]\n\n            while operator_stack:\n                op2_symbol = operator_stack[-1]\n                op2_props = _OP_PROPS[op2_symbol]\n\n                # Pop operators from stack to output if precedence rules allow.\n                if (op2_props['precedence'] > op1_props['precedence']) or \\\n                   (op2_props['precedence'] == op1_props['precedence'] and op1_props['associativity'] == 'left'):\n                    output_queue.append(operator_stack.pop())\n                else:\n                    break\n            operator_stack.append(op1_symbol)\n\n    # Pop any remaining operators from the stack to the output queue.\n    while operator_stack:\n        output_queue.append(operator_stack.pop())\n\n    # Evaluate the RPN expression using a stack.\n    evaluation_stack = []\n    for token in output_queue:\n        if isinstance(token, int):  # If it's an operand, push it onto the evaluation stack.\n            evaluation_stack.append(token)\n        else:  # It's an operator\n            # Pop two operands, apply the operator, and push the result.\n            val2 = evaluation_stack.pop()\n            val1 = evaluation_stack.pop()\n            result = _apply_op(token, val1, val2)\n            evaluation_stack.append(result)\n\n    # The final result is the only item left on the evaluation stack.\n    return evaluation_stack[0]\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/161", "solution": "def solve(s):\n    \"\"\"Transforms a string by reversing letter case or reversing the whole string.\n    If the string contains at least one letter, each letter's case is swapped; otherwise, the entire string is reversed.\n    \"\"\"\n    has_letters = False\n    for char in s:\n        if char.isalpha():\n            has_letters = True\n            break\n\n    if has_letters:\n        transformed_chars = []\n        for char in s:\n            if char.isalpha():\n                if char.islower():\n                    transformed_chars.append(char.upper())\n                else:\n                    transformed_chars.append(char.lower())\n            else:\n                transformed_chars.append(char)\n        return \"\".join(transformed_chars)\n    else:\n        return s[::-1]"}
